WEBVTT

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:47.000
[Opening music]

00:01:20.102 --> 00:01:21.502
The weather's nice.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:27.500
It's warm.

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:35.500
You rascal!

00:01:38.822 --> 00:01:40.222
Out of nowhere.

00:01:44.422 --> 00:01:46.033
What will become of Yu Hamin?

00:01:47.542 --> 00:01:48.942
Bring it on!

00:01:54.022 --> 00:01:55.422
I'll attack you…

00:01:56.142 --> 00:01:57.542
with music!

00:02:04.522 --> 00:02:07.522
Shall I show off my skills for the first time in ages?

00:02:10.542 --> 00:02:11.942
Not so!

00:02:14.182 --> 00:02:15.582
[Sings]

00:02:38.282 --> 00:02:40.281
— There's no sound… — It's okay to scream.

00:02:40.282 --> 00:02:42.482
Nobody. No one's here to hear you.

00:02:46.262 --> 00:02:48.102
[Sings a mangled chant]

00:02:48.562 --> 00:02:51.442
— [Sings, adding ‘Chihuahua’] — There's no sound…

00:02:53.002 --> 00:02:56.242
[Continues the chant]

00:02:56.582 --> 00:03:00.102
[Sings, adding ‘Chihuahua’]

00:03:00.662 --> 00:03:04.242
— What was that? ‘Chihuahua’? — Becaaause…

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:07.500
You rascal!

00:03:09.482 --> 00:03:12.882
Why do you keep saying ‘You rascal!’? Who
are you talking to?

00:03:13.742 --> 00:03:15.142
You rascal!

00:03:15.982 --> 00:03:21.482
— Hey, why are you like this today? — Feeling good
today. — That Buldak ramen's made him act weird.

00:03:22.542 --> 00:03:23.942
What is with you?

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:29.500
Oh, it's over.

00:03:30.642 --> 00:03:32.698
Ja, MC. Get us back on track, please.

00:03:34.582 --> 00:03:35.982
Dear PLLI,

00:03:36.402 --> 00:03:38.342
after about three months…

00:03:38.742 --> 00:03:41.964
— 3 months? — Dear PLLI, after our
three-month world tour,

00:03:42.122 --> 00:03:45.262
we've returned to Asterum in triumph!

00:03:46.122 --> 00:03:47.955
We're PLAVE! A round of applause!

00:03:49.222 --> 00:03:52.242
PLAVE is finally back!

00:03:52.342 --> 00:03:55.701
Great. Let's have a look at the table! Show us.

00:03:55.702 --> 00:04:00.241
— Is this the Last Supper? — Ja, shouldn't
we toast on a happy day like this?

00:04:00.242 --> 00:04:02.821
— Why? — Oh, what should we toast with? — With…

00:04:02.822 --> 00:04:04.600
the pink cocktail I've prepared!

00:04:04.982 --> 00:04:06.742
— A cocktail? — Yogurt?

00:04:08.262 --> 00:04:09.461
Cocktail!

00:04:09.462 --> 00:04:10.862
Come out.

00:04:13.522 --> 00:04:15.721
— Now that's an atmosphere. — Oh, yogurt.

00:04:15.722 --> 00:04:17.642
Ja, a yogurt toast! Cheers!

00:04:18.182 --> 00:04:21.042
We have to toast before we drink.

00:04:21.362 --> 00:04:23.751
You're my hyung, so I'll clink below yours.

00:04:23.882 --> 00:04:29.462
Of course you should. Ja, Yejun, our leader,
give us a toast.

00:04:30.562 --> 00:04:34.142
Ja. I'll keep it short. How about cheongbaji?

00:04:34.322 --> 00:04:36.601
— Ah, great. — Cheongbaji?

00:04:36.602 --> 00:04:40.301
— Know the cheongbaji toast? — A tough one.
— Hyung, that's dated!

00:04:40.302 --> 00:04:42.982
— It's dated? — Very dated. — Really?

00:04:43.082 --> 00:04:45.801
— Let's go. — Go right ahead. — No,
cheongbaji is just right for now.

00:04:45.802 --> 00:04:47.981
— ‘Youth is right now!’ — Exactly! — Right now?

00:04:47.982 --> 00:04:50.581
Ja, one, two, three! Repeat ‘cheongbaji’! — Yes, boss!

00:04:50.582 --> 00:04:52.202
Yes, boss!

00:04:52.562 --> 00:04:55.222
— Yes, boss! — Ja. PLAVE!

00:04:55.322 --> 00:04:59.044
— Cheongbaji! Cheongbaji! — Cheongbaji!
Cheongbaji! — Cheongbajiii!

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:03.400
Ah!

00:05:07.922 --> 00:05:09.322
Ah, nice.

00:05:10.022 --> 00:05:13.001
— Ah, nice. — Sweet, sweet.

00:05:13.002 --> 00:05:15.941
— So sweet! — I do the toast differently. — Sweet.

00:05:15.942 --> 00:05:18.841
— How do you do it again? — You know how
much I love EXO sunbaenim.

00:05:18.842 --> 00:05:23.509
— Really? — How do you do it? — [Turns an
EXO lyric into a ‘raise your glass’ toast]

00:05:25.522 --> 00:05:28.201
— Like this. ‘Raise your glass’? — When did
you rehearse? [Sings]

00:05:28.202 --> 00:05:31.401
— When did you prepare that? — Ja, anyway,
we've had our toast.

00:05:31.402 --> 00:05:34.481
Great. Ja, everyone, please take a seat.

00:05:34.482 --> 00:05:37.101
The chairs are coming in now.

00:05:37.102 --> 00:05:41.621
They're flying right in! You've waited a
long time, everyone. PLAVE's…

00:05:41.622 --> 00:05:43.022
But Bamby…

00:05:43.122 --> 00:05:45.902
You get tipsy so fast, Bamby. Will you be okay?

00:05:47.562 --> 00:05:50.761
— One glass makes me happy. — Ja, sit down!
Hurry! — Isn't it non-alcoholic?

00:05:50.762 --> 00:05:55.301
— I don't drink that much alcohol. — Pull your chairs
forward a bit. — Ja, sit in a line. Everyone line up.

00:05:55.302 --> 00:05:56.361
So noisy! It's been ages.

00:05:56.362 --> 00:06:02.362
Ja, it's been a while, everyone! PLAVE is back. Not that
we ever really left, but seeing you again like this…

00:06:06.362 --> 00:06:12.362
it really feels like ages. Ja, from Munhak to Japan,
Kaohsiung, Bangkok, Singapore, Taipei, Macau and the US!

00:06:17.382 --> 00:06:22.902
Ja, we've finished our long, three-month world tour.

00:06:26.382 --> 00:06:32.382
Let's applaud PLLI who came to see us all over the
world, too. Thank you so much. You worked so hard.

00:06:32.502 --> 00:06:35.341
You really worked hard.

00:06:35.342 --> 00:06:40.041
— PLLI worked so hard, too. Everyone was
amazing. So amazing. — You really did.

00:06:40.042 --> 00:06:43.141
— You were amazing. What a journey. — Yes,
it was awesome.

00:06:43.142 --> 00:06:48.641
Ja, what's changed since last year's Asia Tour? It's worth
looking back. Talking about how we've grown will be fun.

00:06:48.642 --> 00:06:50.042
Sounds good?

00:06:52.342 --> 00:06:56.461
— First, the scale is different. The Asia Tour was
the Asia Tour; this was a world tour. — The culprit?

00:06:56.462 --> 00:06:58.881
World Tour! Ya-ah! We've gone worldwide!

00:06:58.882 --> 00:07:02.161
Worldwide! And the Asia Tour was in 2025.

00:07:02.162 --> 00:07:03.562
What is it?

00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:09.582
The World Tour was in 2026. That's the
biggest difference.

00:07:12.582 --> 00:07:15.821
— That is different. — You're not wrong. —
Quite a difference…

00:07:15.822 --> 00:07:21.382
— A scolding! So educational. — Thanks for
that. — Ja, a different year is important.

00:07:21.642 --> 00:07:23.921
— The biggest difference! — Ja, I didn't expect that.

00:07:23.922 --> 00:07:26.981
— We level up at every concert. — Yes, level up!

00:07:26.982 --> 00:07:29.901
— Level up? What level are we? — Level up! —
What level?

00:07:29.902 --> 00:07:33.013
— This is our third concert, right? — Is
there a number?

00:07:34.162 --> 00:07:35.606
It's the third one, right?

00:07:35.742 --> 00:07:37.353
It's the second tour, though.

00:07:38.062 --> 00:07:41.141
— One level per year's concerts makes three?
— I'd say three.

00:07:41.142 --> 00:07:42.542
3.

00:07:43.542 --> 00:07:46.121
— It could be the fourth time. — 3. — This was Part 3.

00:07:46.122 --> 00:07:49.361
This is Part 3, so we're at Level 3.

00:07:49.362 --> 00:07:52.901
— Ah, three… — But every time the level goes
up. — Uh-huh, it's level 3.

00:07:52.902 --> 00:07:55.662
— Our PLLI are going crazy. — Yo-o!

00:07:55.942 --> 00:08:00.721
The staging has so many surprises and incredible
effects. I heard people went absolutely wild this time.

00:08:00.722 --> 00:08:02.122
Level 3.

00:08:03.242 --> 00:08:06.001
— I hear that a lot. — It was crazy. — My mother said…

00:08:06.002 --> 00:08:09.641
— Your mother! — ‘Your best ever.’ But she says
we outdo ourselves every time. — Your best!

00:08:09.642 --> 00:08:11.042
Whoa-oohhh

00:08:12.022 --> 00:08:15.462
— People I know have said that a lot, too. — Yooohhhhh

00:08:15.822 --> 00:08:19.302
Seriously, actually. Among my friends, well...

00:08:19.502 --> 00:08:22.662
A friend who hadn't been that interested came along.

00:08:22.762 --> 00:08:25.461
Afterward, they really fell for us.

00:08:25.462 --> 00:08:28.742
— A concert that won over new fans! — Yes, really…

00:08:30.482 --> 00:08:36.482
— That's what happened. It felt really
meaningful. — That must feel new.

00:08:37.222 --> 00:08:43.222
I think everyone's stamina has improved a lot, too.
We've learned how to pace ourselves, haven't we?

00:08:45.102 --> 00:08:49.781
— It's experience. We're so in sync now. — Yeah.
The more you do it, the more it feels natural.

00:08:49.782 --> 00:08:51.882
Ah, that's right.

00:08:52.262 --> 00:08:55.441
I didn't cut any corners, but my stamina has improved.

00:08:55.442 --> 00:08:58.001
Really? Have you deleted all your cracked versions?

00:08:58.002 --> 00:09:01.061
— I only eat the original now. — Ya-ah! Original only!

00:09:01.062 --> 00:09:05.302
Original only. Ja, Eunho, you had Buldak ramen today…

00:09:05.682 --> 00:09:09.262
and you seem to be feeling…

00:09:09.482 --> 00:09:13.102
pretty hyped up. Can you share a little TMI?

00:09:14.822 --> 00:09:16.766
You ate it right before the stream.

00:09:17.002 --> 00:09:19.541
— Wiping your nose! — He kept going ‘ss-ha, ss-ha.’

00:09:19.542 --> 00:09:22.875
— You kept huffing and puffing. — ‘Ss-ha,
ss-ha,’ like this.

00:09:23.762 --> 00:09:26.001
— He kept doing that. — Uh, now — How are you feeling?

00:09:26.002 --> 00:09:28.461
— It's killing me! Honestly, that Buldak… — Really?

00:09:28.462 --> 00:09:31.721
— Why eat it if you can't handle spice? — I
don't get it!

00:09:31.722 --> 00:09:34.282
But I can handle spicy food… I'm good with it!

00:09:34.382 --> 00:09:37.522
Something's wrong with this one. Was it expired?

00:09:37.682 --> 00:09:39.541
— Did that make it spicier? — It expired?

00:09:39.542 --> 00:09:43.598
I don't think that's it. You need to
negotiate with your internal organs.

00:09:45.002 --> 00:09:47.222
Ja, anyway… TMI?

00:09:47.402 --> 00:09:49.382
Today's TMI…

00:09:49.942 --> 00:09:51.342
We're going to

00:09:51.542 --> 00:09:53.042
Uh... Today?

00:09:53.422 --> 00:09:54.761
Earlier...

00:09:54.762 --> 00:09:56.484
we did a test broadcast, right?

00:09:57.482 --> 00:10:03.482
We'll be showing you lots of different sides
of ourselves. That's my TMI.

00:10:05.782 --> 00:10:10.001
— TMI. — Yejun-hyung really wants to show
you different sides.

00:10:10.002 --> 00:10:11.941
— Really? — Quieter streams show a different side.

00:10:11.942 --> 00:10:14.342
Casual streams, yes.

00:10:18.502 --> 00:10:20.001
Different kinds of content…

00:10:20.002 --> 00:10:23.762
We could make other kinds of content, too.
It sounds fun.

00:10:24.142 --> 00:10:26.586
From what I hear, there's a lot we could do.

00:10:27.242 --> 00:10:28.642
That's all.

00:10:30.702 --> 00:10:33.641
— That's what I heard. — From what we heard.
What we heard.

00:10:33.642 --> 00:10:38.741
It's still in development. Please look forward to it.

00:10:38.742 --> 00:10:44.742
— Okay. — Great. — We each prepared remarks
in the local languages, too.

00:10:45.522 --> 00:10:50.999
— Do it. Yeah, that's right. — It was such a
meaningful experience.

00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:55.441
When else would we visit those places and
speak their languages?

00:10:55.442 --> 00:10:58.962
— Yeah, right. How was it? — How was it, Noah?

00:11:01.102 --> 00:11:02.769
Preparing the closing remarks?

00:11:03.182 --> 00:11:08.782
Preparing those remarks… I wanted to share my sincere…

00:11:09.162 --> 00:11:15.162
honest feelings. I thought it'd be nice to say them in
each city's language. I hadn't thought of it at first.

00:11:15.922 --> 00:11:18.821
— You hadn't? When did you think of it? — I
got the idea when…

00:11:18.822 --> 00:11:20.522
— Yejun… — Yejun!

00:11:21.102 --> 00:11:24.201
— was speaking in Chinese. — He prepared a
lot of Chinese. — Ah, Chinese. Right.

00:11:24.202 --> 00:11:28.362
That look... Beside me, he looked so adorable.

00:11:28.902 --> 00:11:31.761
How can someone be this adorable?

00:11:31.762 --> 00:11:34.595
— Really? — I thought, ‘I should be adorable, too!’

00:11:34.762 --> 00:11:40.762
So I prepared some. Then, as we started doing it
one by one, everyone caught on, and all five of us…

00:11:43.542 --> 00:11:46.961
— That's how it turned out. — Yes. — Noah,
did you prepare first?

00:11:46.962 --> 00:11:50.022
Was I third? Second? Were you second?

00:11:50.582 --> 00:11:53.081
— Second… When was it? — I can't remember.

00:11:53.082 --> 00:11:55.781
— We've visited so many cities. — So many… —
You're getting quieter!

00:11:55.782 --> 00:12:01.742
— I'm allowed to forget! — Anyway, we all
wanted to express the same feelings.

00:12:01.862 --> 00:12:07.862
Let's put it that way. Your own language
touches you more.

00:12:08.662 --> 00:12:11.861
— Right. — Our skills weren't great. Thanks
for understanding and finding us cute.

00:12:11.862 --> 00:12:14.641
— Thank you so much. — Thank you. By city, maybe…

00:12:14.642 --> 00:12:20.642
Does anyone remember a phrase from one of
the cities we visited?

00:12:21.522 --> 00:12:24.381
— Any of the things we said? — M-thang-oh! Sui-lah!

00:12:24.382 --> 00:12:26.761
— M-thang-oh! Sui-lah, sui-lah, sui-lah! —
Ha! M-thang-oh!

00:12:26.762 --> 00:12:28.181
— Sui-lah! — Seung-il! — Sui-lah!

00:12:28.182 --> 00:12:31.293
— Sui-lah! Did you ever find this ‘Sui-lah’?
— Seung-il!

00:12:31.562 --> 00:12:35.301
I thought you were calling some friend, like
Kim Su-il. You suddenly went ‘Sui-lah! Sui-lah!’

00:12:35.302 --> 00:12:38.181
— Seung-il! Hey, Seung-il! — Sui-lah! — But
there's a tone to it, too.

00:12:38.182 --> 00:12:39.582
Hyung, you try it, too.

00:12:39.602 --> 00:12:42.001
— ‘Sui-lah’ means ‘Awesome’, right? — Sui-lah!

00:12:42.002 --> 00:12:43.721
— Yeah… — I think so. Sui-lah! — Sui-lah!

00:12:43.722 --> 00:12:44.761
Sui-lah!

00:12:44.762 --> 00:12:47.141
— M-thang-oh! M-thang-oh! — Sui-lah! — M-thang-oh!

00:12:47.142 --> 00:12:49.802
That means ‘Don't do that.’

00:12:50.802 --> 00:12:53.141
— That's already been a month, isn't it? — Already?

00:12:53.142 --> 00:12:55.121
— Right? — Wow, it's flying by! — It really is.

00:12:55.122 --> 00:12:57.621
Really? We've been so busy, I lost track of time.

00:12:57.622 --> 00:13:02.482
Ah, Seung-il! Actually, can I tell you
something surprising?

00:13:02.742 --> 00:13:04.142
Suddenly?

00:13:05.202 --> 00:13:09.581
— Why is the flow like this? — Bamby's
unsmooth hosting is part of his charm.

00:13:09.582 --> 00:13:14.321
— Oh, really — Right, it's so bouncy—like fish roe.
— It's all over the place! That's fun. Dopamine!

00:13:14.322 --> 00:13:16.461
— Say something surprising. — Surprise us!

00:13:16.462 --> 00:13:18.422
I already missed the timing.

00:13:18.802 --> 00:13:21.581
— Was there an opening? — I can't say now. —
Find another opening!

00:13:21.582 --> 00:13:22.701
— Opening? — Tell us later.

00:13:22.702 --> 00:13:25.462
The bus has already left.

00:13:25.642 --> 00:13:27.142
Right. It's not a big deal.

00:13:27.502 --> 00:13:31.861
— Ja, let's move on, everyone. Moving on. — Yes.
Good. Good. Good. Yes. — Ah, okay, that's great.

00:13:31.862 --> 00:13:34.481
— M-thang-oh! — Ja, everyone, did you know?

00:13:34.482 --> 00:13:39.082
— What? — It's already November 2026.

00:13:39.922 --> 00:13:43.533
— Oh, I knew it. — Of course. November 17!
Ja! — You know, right?

00:13:43.602 --> 00:13:47.041
So, What's happening in November?

00:13:47.042 --> 00:13:50.381
In November... We have the MMA. Right, MMA!

00:13:50.382 --> 00:13:53.361
Did you watch the MMA? MMA! I was about to
talk about our MMA performance.

00:13:53.362 --> 00:13:55.121
Ah. Everyone.

00:13:55.122 --> 00:13:58.801
Double denim! So hot now. Not everyone can
pull it off. Ja, the clothes first.

00:13:58.802 --> 00:14:00.322
Double denim.

00:14:05.122 --> 00:14:09.622
Let's change outfits, everyone. Ja, one, two, three!

00:14:11.302 --> 00:14:13.702
Ja, this is our denim.

00:14:13.862 --> 00:14:16.541
It's a light-colored denim, with a lot of washing.

00:14:16.542 --> 00:14:18.999
— It's been heavily washed. — Got it.

00:14:19.000 --> 00:14:21.499
I love this shade.

00:14:21.500 --> 00:14:24.499
Ja, you probably never imagined denim like this.

00:14:24.500 --> 00:14:28.862
Ja, great. At the MMA…

00:14:29.222 --> 00:14:32.402
And that traditional-style Watch Me Woo…

00:14:32.522 --> 00:14:37.702
We'd only done it at our concert. PLLI
didn't expect to see it at the MMA.

00:14:38.062 --> 00:14:44.062
I watch a lot of PLLI reaction videos. You know,
where they film themselves watching? At that moment…

00:14:48.502 --> 00:14:50.002
they were really surprised.

00:14:50.542 --> 00:14:51.942
This one.

00:14:52.882 --> 00:14:56.262
I guess that tiger was too good to keep just
to ourselves.

00:14:56.462 --> 00:14:59.462
It reminded me how much they liked it…

00:14:59.702 --> 00:15:00.821
That came to mind.

00:15:00.822 --> 00:15:03.921
— ‘It came to mind.’ That's what he means. —
It came to mind. Came to mind.

00:15:03.922 --> 00:15:05.701
— Eunho, stop laughing! — I don't like it.

00:15:05.702 --> 00:15:09.222
— Why? I didn't do anything! — Why. Why. Why.

00:15:11.502 --> 00:15:14.021
— Too good! — Forgive him. He's had Buldak. — Why?

00:15:14.022 --> 00:15:16.621
— Great energy today. — Extra spicy!

00:15:16.622 --> 00:15:18.761
You're doing so well, I can't help laughing. Really!

00:15:18.762 --> 00:15:23.182
Thank you. Ja, Eunho, explain how you
brought that tiger along.

00:15:26.462 --> 00:15:30.001
— The tiger! How did you bring it? — I'm
thrifty. — How did you bring it?

00:15:30.002 --> 00:15:32.461
— All the way from LA. — How did the tiger
travel? — From LA.

00:15:32.462 --> 00:15:35.502
If you're asking how it traveled…

00:15:35.602 --> 00:15:38.102
obviously, the tiger came with me…

00:15:38.222 --> 00:15:41.041
— through the Anywhere Door. — The Anywhere
Door! — Yes, through that.

00:15:41.042 --> 00:15:44.162
What's that thing called?

00:15:44.322 --> 00:15:46.861
— The thing you put on dogs… — Har… har…

00:15:46.862 --> 00:15:48.781
— A harness. — A harness, is it? — Harness

00:15:48.782 --> 00:15:51.341
— A harness? — Did it wear one? — A harness?
— No harness?

00:15:51.342 --> 00:15:54.941
— No harness. I can control it with hand
signals. I don't need one. — You didn't?

00:15:54.942 --> 00:15:57.164
— Ah. With a hand gesture. — You didn't?

00:15:58.902 --> 00:16:01.141
When I gesture like this, it comes over to me.

00:16:01.142 --> 00:16:03.781
— A pet tiger! A pet tiger. — With a whistle

00:16:03.782 --> 00:16:06.321
Yes, exactly. And when I say ‘Sit!’…

00:16:06.322 --> 00:16:08.581
— ‘Sit’! — You taught it English, not Korean?

00:16:08.582 --> 00:16:10.342
In English.

00:16:11.082 --> 00:16:13.661
In English. It had to adapt to being in LA.

00:16:13.662 --> 00:16:16.162
Ah. That's right. That's right.

00:16:17.002 --> 00:16:20.042
