00:29:37.622 --> 00:29:40.182
Usually, foundation is… That's it.

00:29:40.422 --> 00:29:41.641
— Cushion. — Foundation?

00:29:41.642 --> 00:29:45.061
— Cushion foundation differs from BB? — The
one you pat on.

00:29:45.062 --> 00:29:47.601
— Different. It changes your tone. — Yes, different.

00:29:47.602 --> 00:29:51.562
— BB cream makes you paler. — Both change
your tone. — My foundation…

00:29:51.782 --> 00:29:54.121
— Foundation changes tone, too. — No cushion for me.

00:29:54.122 --> 00:29:56.781
— I use a brush, like this. — Oh, I didn't know that.

00:29:56.782 --> 00:29:58.381
— Foundation. — With a brush? — Oh, that!

00:29:58.382 --> 00:30:01.461
— Yes, they use it at the makeup salon. —
Like that, squeezing it...

00:30:01.462 --> 00:30:03.761
— Foundation: full makeup. — BB: put it on and go.

00:30:03.762 --> 00:30:06.761
— You can see it that way. — BB's the easy option.

00:30:06.762 --> 00:30:09.381
— BB cream doesn't have separate shade
numbers. — Ah. Really?

00:30:09.382 --> 00:30:12.721
— Ah. Really? — There aren't that many
shades. But… — Oh, no shade options.

00:30:12.722 --> 00:30:15.061
— Foundation has more shades to match your
skin. — Really?

00:30:15.062 --> 00:30:16.462
Oh, really.

00:30:16.942 --> 00:30:19.281
— CC? — BB mixed with sunscreen. — I was curious.

00:30:19.282 --> 00:30:20.682
CC is sunscreen?

00:30:21.302 --> 00:30:23.621
— Sunscreen? — BB plus sunscreen. — I
wondered about that.

00:30:23.622 --> 00:30:25.322
CC looks natural, though.

00:30:25.942 --> 00:30:30.441
— CC cream. — I like CC. — BB cream mixed with
sunscreen. — If you combine BB and sunscreen…

00:30:30.442 --> 00:30:33.302
— Shouldn't it be BS? — That's what I heard CC was.

00:30:33.522 --> 00:30:34.922
Oh, really?

00:30:35.702 --> 00:30:40.201
— Could you show someone other than me? —
Why do you have to come here specifically?

00:30:40.202 --> 00:30:44.681
— Why, why. Why? — Right here. — Why did you suddenly
run over there all by yourself? — Huh, why suddenly?

00:30:44.682 --> 00:30:49.521
— I needed a moment to collect myself. Yes. —
I thought my eyes were playing tricks on me.

00:30:49.522 --> 00:30:52.361
Ja, Noah's been studying makeup a lot lately.

00:30:52.362 --> 00:30:57.901
— It's not sunscreen, right? Ah. You're studying? —
So now, after getting a lot of info from PLLI, I'll

00:30:57.902 --> 00:31:01.742
I'm really lazy about this stuff, you see.

00:31:02.122 --> 00:31:05.622
— Actually, I just end up not doing it
again. — You really are.

00:31:06.062 --> 00:31:07.462
What did you say?

00:31:08.182 --> 00:31:09.702
No no, just ignore it

00:31:10.502 --> 00:31:12.141
— What are you saying? — What?

00:31:12.142 --> 00:31:14.441
— Never mind. Can't be bothered. — What's this?

00:31:14.442 --> 00:31:16.999
— What? What's this bit? Anyway… — Ah,
anyway, because of that

00:31:17.000 --> 00:31:21.499
PLLI gave me so much information. I wanted
to study it properly.

00:31:21.500 --> 00:31:24.441
I don't have any hobbies, you know.

00:31:24.442 --> 00:31:28.761
I don't play games, so I thought I'd try
makeup as a hobby. That's why I'm doing it now.

00:31:28.762 --> 00:31:33.681
— Makeup hobby! — Fun! — No progress since
then, but I'll give it a try.

00:31:33.682 --> 00:31:36.881
— Thinking about it? — Yes. — Not opening a
salon in three years, are you?

00:31:36.882 --> 00:31:39.121
— Will you end up making cosmetics? — Later…

00:31:39.122 --> 00:31:42.321
— Amazing! — Just as a hobby? A cosmetics business?!

00:31:42.322 --> 00:31:43.821
— Not a business? — Could be.

00:31:43.822 --> 00:31:46.441
— Who knows if I get into it? Not now, though. — Why?

00:31:46.442 --> 00:31:47.842
If you get into it…

00:31:49.962 --> 00:31:54.602
I only need three things to get ready every
day. Just three.

00:31:54.682 --> 00:31:58.982
— Which one? — Dashu, Mise-en-scène… Dashu,
Mise-en-scène…

00:31:59.242 --> 00:32:02.601
— Hair products? — Those are brands… —
Gatsby. Those three are all I need.

00:32:02.602 --> 00:32:04.822
You used all three on your hair today?

00:32:05.362 --> 00:32:07.281
— What about Dashu? — Apply it here.

00:32:07.282 --> 00:32:09.004
You're putting on way too much.

00:32:09.302 --> 00:32:12.561
— Here. — We've seen Eunho get ready. Under
five minutes!

00:32:12.562 --> 00:32:13.962
What?

00:32:17.042 --> 00:32:19.221
— He barely does anything. — Oh, seriously.

00:32:19.222 --> 00:32:20.461
Different. But foundation…

00:32:20.462 --> 00:32:24.461
— I do apply it! — Ah. But foundation on the
face. — But it doesn't get patchy!

00:32:24.462 --> 00:32:28.742
— Even without lotion. Noah-hyung was
shocked. — Just really face.

00:32:28.822 --> 00:32:31.401
He puts foundation on in about thirty seconds. Right?

00:32:31.402 --> 00:32:34.101
— Know what's funny? — Just that much. — What's funny?

00:32:34.102 --> 00:32:36.921
Eunho contours, too. Oh, did we tell this story?

00:32:36.922 --> 00:32:39.701
— He even contours? — I contour. — I told
that story ages ago.

00:32:39.702 --> 00:32:41.941
— Contour here? — I do. — Already told it!

00:32:41.942 --> 00:32:44.241
Tell them how. I have my own contouring technique.

00:32:44.242 --> 00:32:47.499
He has a technique: foundation or BB cream
all over his face.

00:32:47.500 --> 00:32:49.999
He goes really pale.

00:32:50.000 --> 00:32:54.221
Then: ‘Watch how I contour.’ With his clean hand…

00:32:54.222 --> 00:33:00.222
he rubs along his jaw like this to sculpt
it. Then along his nose, like this.

00:33:00.902 --> 00:33:05.101
— Like this, like this. Like this. — And it
actually creates shadows!

00:33:05.102 --> 00:33:07.381
— That's what contouring is. — Wow. So macho.

00:33:07.382 --> 00:33:11.241
— Rumor has it he peels his makeup off from
the bottom. — He just peels off a whole layer.

00:33:11.242 --> 00:33:14.181
— Like peeling off a sheet mask. — Ah. Peel
it off. Peel it off.

00:33:14.182 --> 00:33:15.441
— Peel off sheets! — Let's!

00:33:15.442 --> 00:33:18.661
— It sets, then he peels it off. — Just peel
the skin! — Skin!

00:33:18.662 --> 00:33:21.942
Disposable. Disposable. Disposable.

00:33:22.422 --> 00:33:25.202
Thinly. Like plastic wrap. Right.

00:33:25.782 --> 00:33:30.601
— Oh. Anyway. — Eunho, you do use cleansing
oil to wash it off, right?

00:33:30.602 --> 00:33:36.602
— Cleansing oil's only for heavy, layered stage
makeup or eyes… — He washes it off the next day!

00:33:38.762 --> 00:33:42.341
— Actually, I don't use eye makeup remover,
either. — You don't remove it, do you?

00:33:42.342 --> 00:33:45.061
— Just cleansing foam? — Even on my eyes, like this.

00:33:45.062 --> 00:33:46.462
I'm...

00:33:47.542 --> 00:33:53.542
I do it all at once like this. If I've got eye makeup on,
I squeeze out a little more and go over my eyes again.

00:33:54.502 --> 00:33:56.741
— But it's not a lie—really. — Rub it in. No, really.

00:33:56.742 --> 00:34:00.582
I remember doing back-to-back schedules with
Eunho, that's all.

00:34:00.742 --> 00:34:04.361
— Next day, the makeup artist touched it up
instead of redoing it. — That's how!

00:34:04.362 --> 00:34:06.901
— What? — Just touch-ups. — I've seen it happen.

00:34:06.902 --> 00:34:11.341
— Oh, really? — That's right. That's how it's
done. — Eunho, is there a reason you do that?

00:34:11.342 --> 00:34:12.742
Oh.

00:34:13.202 --> 00:34:14.661
— Such a hassle. — Too much hassle.

00:34:14.662 --> 00:34:17.301
Because my skin doesn't break out even if I do that.

00:34:17.302 --> 00:34:19.601
— How is your skin undamaged? — Yes. — It's cast iron!

00:34:19.602 --> 00:34:22.121
— What? — Ah, I'm really worried, that's why
I'm saying this

00:34:22.122 --> 00:34:23.601
— His skin really is fine. — I…

00:34:23.602 --> 00:34:27.102
— If it breaks out… — Your skin's amazing
right now, seriously.

00:34:27.722 --> 00:34:33.041
— You need to take care of it. — If it suddenly goes
downhill, I'll accept it as my fate. — Ah, destiny?

00:34:33.042 --> 00:34:36.681
— I actually tried copying him once and it
went horribly wrong. — It's wild.

00:34:36.682 --> 00:34:39.701
— His skin used to be even better. — If it
goes downhill, that's fate.

00:34:39.702 --> 00:34:41.782
Destiny can't be defied, that's why.

00:34:41.942 --> 00:34:44.164
Meeting you was also part of my destiny.

00:34:44.682 --> 00:34:46.222
— Understood. — Thank you.

00:34:47.342 --> 00:34:49.201
— Move on. — Ja, the topic? — Can't win.

00:34:49.202 --> 00:34:50.421
— Weverse. Next? — No idea.

00:34:50.422 --> 00:34:53.361
— Your approach. — Oh, right. — What do you
actually do?

00:34:53.362 --> 00:34:56.421
— We know Hamin's approach. Who else? —
Yejun, what's yours?

00:34:56.422 --> 00:35:01.261
I'm completely spontaneous. I just go live
without a plan. ‘What are you doing?’

00:35:01.262 --> 00:35:02.662
P, P. A total P!

00:35:03.282 --> 00:35:05.999
— That's right. — That's how I start. —
That's such a P thing.

00:35:06.000 --> 00:35:10.999
Maybe I'll sing a song, or look for
something fun online.

00:35:11.000 --> 00:35:15.301
— Search Naver, browse together… — Naver,
let me check it out. Hmm.

00:35:15.302 --> 00:35:17.521
‘Apparently there's this place in Gyeongsang
Province.’

00:35:17.522 --> 00:35:19.821
— Like chatting on the phone. — ‘There's
this in Jeolla.’

00:35:19.822 --> 00:35:23.021
— Like chatting with a friend. — Just… — I
wrote it, then… Hmm.

00:35:23.022 --> 00:35:25.321
Then if I have somewhere to be, ‘I'm off now.’

00:35:25.322 --> 00:35:27.921
— What, like this — Hey, decisively — Oh,
very decisively.

00:35:27.922 --> 00:35:30.161
— Plain and simple. — Simple! — Plain and simple.

00:35:30.162 --> 00:35:35.501
— It's plain and simple. — But I'd like to
try something properly planned, with a script.

00:35:35.502 --> 00:35:38.921
— It doesn't work well. — Ah, writing the
script? — Shall I handle the planning a bit?

00:35:38.922 --> 00:35:41.621
— Yes, that's good. — That's nice. — Leave it to me.

00:35:41.622 --> 00:35:43.441
— I do that, too. — I'd like a consultation.

00:35:43.442 --> 00:35:49.442
I'm spontaneous, too. No plan. I just decide
to go live and turn it on.

00:35:50.922 --> 00:35:52.322
You can really tell.

00:35:53.802 --> 00:35:55.202
After turning it on

00:35:56.102 --> 00:35:57.481
Ah, that's right.

00:35:57.482 --> 00:36:00.721
You think of something after going live.
That's your charm, hyung.

00:36:00.722 --> 00:36:03.281
— Not teasing! — It's beyond off-the-cuff. — Funny!

00:36:03.282 --> 00:36:06.221
— It's like you accidentally hit the button.
— Hahaha. Stop it. — Yeah. Oh.

00:36:06.222 --> 00:36:08.461
‘Oh, Weverse Live…’

00:36:08.462 --> 00:36:10.981
He actually says, ‘Oh? It's on?’

00:36:10.982 --> 00:36:13.462
— ‘Hi, PLLI.’ — Do this one. — ‘Hello.’

00:36:13.542 --> 00:36:14.942
And keep going

00:36:15.062 --> 00:36:18.006
— Ah, the sound of breathing, breathing — ‘Hi, PLLI.’

00:36:18.062 --> 00:36:19.951
Why do you keep making this sound?

00:36:20.982 --> 00:36:23.761
— No, I think that's content. — So, — Yeah.

00:36:23.762 --> 00:36:25.161
— Bonggu's content! — That noise?

00:36:25.162 --> 00:36:28.181
I don't know! Why am I the only one whose
breathing gets picked up?

00:36:28.182 --> 00:36:30.641
— That is. — Ah, say it like this.

00:36:30.642 --> 00:36:33.142
Are you holding your phone against your nose?

00:36:33.942 --> 00:36:36.622
— Why always do that? — Really? — Why just me?

00:36:36.822 --> 00:36:39.501
— That's really weird. — [Breathy imitation]
Did you eat?

00:36:39.502 --> 00:36:43.861
— Are you holding it really close? Why? —
When I'm sitting down, with a table like this…

00:36:43.862 --> 00:36:47.122
— I think I know. — Reading comments with
your phone here…

00:36:47.182 --> 00:36:48.841
— Bad eyesight? Why so close? — Like this.

00:36:48.842 --> 00:36:51.861
— No need to sit so far away. — I think that's why.

00:36:51.862 --> 00:36:53.262
Just stay still.

00:36:53.502 --> 00:36:55.861
— Usually in the living room? — How'd you know?

00:36:55.862 --> 00:36:57.862
— Living room… — Yes, I do it there.

00:36:58.402 --> 00:37:01.882
— There's a sofa here. Do you sit on it like
this? — Right.

00:37:02.262 --> 00:37:04.942
But my couch is actually right here.

00:37:05.222 --> 00:37:07.201
— About this high. The table here. — Really?

00:37:07.202 --> 00:37:08.602
Then this one...

00:37:09.042 --> 00:37:12.341
— Hold it or put it on the table? — On the
table. Like this.

00:37:12.342 --> 00:37:14.321
— Of course your face ends up close. — I see!

00:37:14.322 --> 00:37:15.878
That's why it picks that up.

00:37:16.782 --> 00:37:20.261
— Oh, is that comfortable? — That's it. — No,
just show me the posture once. I'm curious.

00:37:20.262 --> 00:37:23.121
— How do you lay it flat? — Just show me!

00:37:23.122 --> 00:37:26.341
— How do you even do that? — You're just
keeping it like this? For over an hour?

00:37:26.342 --> 00:37:32.141
— It's because your shoulders are weak. You can't
hold its weight, can you? It's too tiring. — Really?

00:37:32.142 --> 00:37:36.301
Ah, it's not because it's hard. It's just
comfortable like this. Watching like this.

00:37:36.302 --> 00:37:41.621
— Ah, seriously frustrating. — Ah, I just don't get
it. Seriously? — You need to do some front raises.

00:37:41.622 --> 00:37:44.601
— Seriously. — Shoulder — What is it? — I'll
show you one way.

00:37:44.602 --> 00:37:47.522
— Your phone's lying flat. Do this. — Flat!

00:37:47.542 --> 00:37:50.709
— The mic. Got it. — Just one like that. —
Is this right?

00:37:50.822 --> 00:37:53.521
— It's right here. — The mic's by the
charger. — Got it.

00:37:53.522 --> 00:37:55.761
— No need to change it. — That was part of the charm.

00:37:55.762 --> 00:37:58.102
— Your own way, hyung. — That's the charm!

00:37:58.742 --> 00:38:01.701
— I do that. — Show us once. — The nose flute?

00:38:01.702 --> 00:38:06.869
— Just show me once. Show me exactly how to do
the pose. — I said the sofa was low, didn't I?

00:38:08.022 --> 00:38:10.701
— Like this, really like this. — I said I
couldn't recreate it here.

00:38:10.702 --> 00:38:13.641
— Can't recreate it? — Eunho, my sofa's
lower. I showed you.

00:38:13.642 --> 00:38:17.841
— Yeah. Right there. — This isn't working, is
it? — I can't do that here. This sofa's higher.

00:38:17.842 --> 00:38:20.982
Oh, so this is what swearing with your eyes means.

00:38:21.162 --> 00:38:25.961
— No, this isn't working at all. — I'm sorry.
— You're really getting on my nerves today.

00:38:25.962 --> 00:38:29.101
— Switch seats with Yejun? — Later. — No way!

00:38:29.102 --> 00:38:31.941
— I need a buffer. — Yes, you need one! — A shield.

00:38:31.942 --> 00:38:35.661
— Yeah. I need one. — Why? — Anyway, we
haven't heard Eunho's approach yet.

00:38:35.662 --> 00:38:39.881
— Well... I'm just... What? — Eunho, you always
have a concept. Last time, bulgogi or something?

00:38:39.882 --> 00:38:42.441
— Cooking: he plans things. — Beef! — Beef?

00:38:42.442 --> 00:38:45.442
— Plan beforehand? — They do. — I don't plan anything.

00:38:45.582 --> 00:38:46.982
I'm improvising.

00:38:47.062 --> 00:38:49.581
— Spontaneous, too. — Yes, whatever comes to mind.

00:38:49.582 --> 00:38:52.262
Ah, what should I even say? How do I put this?

00:38:52.402 --> 00:38:58.402
So I just, well... I told PLLI the other members
are so good at talking, unlike me. They're so…

00:39:01.222 --> 00:39:03.602
smooth about it. Like slippery eels.

00:39:03.702 --> 00:39:06.646
— At chatting. No, I mean the members. — Is that you?

00:39:06.982 --> 00:39:09.441
— ‘Mem-buhs.’ — Members. — ‘Mem-buhs’?! —
Mem… members.

00:39:09.442 --> 00:39:15.442
— The members. — They read comments, and even when
there's a pause, it doesn't feel awkward. — The members.

00:39:15.982 --> 00:39:18.760
They're really good at this. Bamby, you're just...

00:39:18.982 --> 00:39:21.941
— Lots of dead air for me. — You're so
unbothered! How?

00:39:21.942 --> 00:39:23.342
Don't you like it?

00:39:25.042 --> 00:39:27.821
— Like content for quiet contemplation? — Anyway…

00:39:27.822 --> 00:39:29.222
Yeah.

00:39:29.502 --> 00:39:33.621
— You listen to music, then if you're bored…
— Listening, then suddenly singing.

00:39:33.622 --> 00:39:36.222
you get something out of the fridge to eat.

00:39:36.342 --> 00:39:41.786
There are times when you run out of things to say,
right? ‘What now?’ So I just read the comments…

00:39:41.802 --> 00:39:44.981
and sit quietly until I find one I want to respond to.

00:39:44.982 --> 00:39:47.222
— Wow, really? — What?

00:39:47.442 --> 00:39:49.782
I hardly ever have any dead air.

00:39:50.002 --> 00:39:52.821
— Oh, so a pause is possible. — What do you
mean, "better"?

00:39:52.822 --> 00:39:58.002
Noah-hyung really doesn't have any. He keeps
things flowing.

00:39:58.582 --> 00:40:01.141
— Your voice isn't… — Without talking, it's
pat-pat-pat.

00:40:01.142 --> 00:40:04.661
— This? — And the hair dryer! — You kept
asking for it again!

00:40:04.662 --> 00:40:09.201
— Oh, you did the get ready with me thing again
too. Uh. — I genuinely dry my hair on stream.

00:40:09.202 --> 00:40:13.821
— Five minutes of nothing but hair-dryer noise. —
Really? What else? I've even put laundry out to dry.

00:40:13.822 --> 00:40:16.501
— Laundry? How far did you go? — Wow. — It
was in the washer.

00:40:16.502 --> 00:40:18.169
You've put laundry out to dry?

00:40:18.500 --> 00:40:22.322
I'd forgotten it was running. Then it went…

00:40:22.482 --> 00:40:25.101
— It's ringing! — Yes. — Ding-ding-dong!

00:40:25.102 --> 00:40:28.621
— but like... — ‘Go hang it up!’ — PLLI kept
saying, ‘Go hang it up!’

00:40:28.622 --> 00:40:31.441
— ‘Really? Can I?’ So I did. —
Ding-ding-ding-dong-dong-dong-dong-dong

00:40:31.442 --> 00:40:35.761
— Wow. This is amazing. But... — Laundry
too. — You don't put everything in the dryer?

00:40:35.762 --> 00:40:39.462
Things like T-shirts that can't go in the dryer.

00:40:39.622 --> 00:40:42.442
— So, — I shook them out and put them up to dry.

00:40:43.002 --> 00:40:45.941
— I put absolutely everything in the dryer.
— That's amazing.

00:40:45.942 --> 00:40:48.181
— Dryer. — Eunho So anyway,

00:40:48.182 --> 00:40:54.182
I go live spontaneously, but then I feel pressure
to do something. What should I talk about?

00:40:55.142 --> 00:40:57.901
— Why? — That's probably a bit of a
professional habit.

00:40:57.902 --> 00:40:59.661
— Have to entertain. — I get it.

00:40:59.662 --> 00:41:02.182
— Ah, I gotta say something. — That is...

00:41:03.062 --> 00:41:06.101
I feel that pressure. PLLI like my singing.
I'm a singer.

00:41:06.102 --> 00:41:09.999
— Ah, but that's exactly the content. — So I
keep singing to avoid dead air.

00:41:10.000 --> 00:41:12.802
They like cooking, so I cook.

00:41:14.862 --> 00:41:20.201
But I did prepare a concept this time. That
‘Sogogi’ one we mentioned. Busking on Weverse…

00:41:20.202 --> 00:41:21.602
What, did you make steak?

00:41:22.662 --> 00:41:25.961
— It wasn't Burger King. — Weverse plus
busking: ‘We-busking.’

00:41:25.962 --> 00:41:27.362
Ah, busking.

00:41:28.000 --> 00:41:32.542
I played an unknown pre-debut singer called
Sogogi—Beef.

00:41:33.362 --> 00:41:36.022
I picked Sogogi as my stage name.

00:41:36.362 --> 00:41:38.902
So, before my debut…

00:41:39.702 --> 00:41:42.021
— I'd be busking on the street. — If you're
going to do it.

00:41:42.022 --> 00:41:46.901
— Going back in time. — So, — Yeah, this is
