00:54:13.342 --> 00:54:14.961
— No, don't buy any. — Let's not!

00:54:14.962 --> 00:54:17.621
Then I'll look stupid! Don't buy any. Same
level is fine, but…

00:54:17.622 --> 00:54:20.362
— Let's not do it. — You can buy one, too, hyung.

00:54:24.882 --> 00:54:28.661
— If one's too good, the others look weak. —
They'd look bad. — I'm worried.

00:54:28.662 --> 00:54:32.081
— Yeah, hyung. Be honest with me. — You
can't help feeling that way.

00:54:32.082 --> 00:54:34.601
— Really… — I'm worried. — Okay, I get it.

00:54:34.602 --> 00:54:37.461
— Okay. Just right for the team's image. —
Understood. — Great.

00:54:37.462 --> 00:54:41.021
It's live. We can't edit any of it out.

00:54:41.022 --> 00:54:42.061
— Live: no edits! — Right!

00:54:42.062 --> 00:54:45.621
— No. It all goes out as it is. — We're just
too exposed, you know.

00:54:45.622 --> 00:54:48.421
— Dangerous! — Great. Ja, Hamin's birthday stream!

00:54:48.422 --> 00:54:49.962
Good. Ja.

00:54:54.322 --> 00:54:57.342
Caligo made his first appearance.

00:54:57.582 --> 00:55:02.341
What did you think? I know Caligo a little.
He's pretty good on stream.

00:55:02.342 --> 00:55:06.731
— Oh, you all watched it. Is there anyone
who didn't? — Caligo. Yes. Of course.

00:55:07.182 --> 00:55:09.781
— Got something to say? — Oh no, not really.
— Again, no way?

00:55:09.782 --> 00:55:11.182
Wow, Noah-ssi

00:55:14.582 --> 00:55:16.301
— Ask about the stream. — Hear me out.

00:55:16.302 --> 00:55:19.541
I was looking at Noah when I asked. He
wouldn't meet my eyes at all.

00:55:19.542 --> 00:55:21.002
— Ask him. — Really.

00:55:22.382 --> 00:55:23.782
Avoiding eye contact.

00:55:25.782 --> 00:55:30.981
Noah-hyung, if you watched Hamin's stream,
do you know what he did?

00:55:30.982 --> 00:55:33.201
— Name Shorts you've seen. — I know! — What?

00:55:33.202 --> 00:55:36.101
You played Tekken.

00:55:36.102 --> 00:55:37.421
And

00:55:37.422 --> 00:55:38.822
Okay.

00:55:41.862 --> 00:55:44.622
And you talked with Caligo.

00:55:46.662 --> 00:55:48.062
When Caligo's not around

00:55:48.142 --> 00:55:52.422
Caligo… And Hamin's happiness gauge.

00:55:52.942 --> 00:55:54.741
— No! — Knows the happiness gauge! He watched!

00:55:54.742 --> 00:55:57.261
— I know, right? — I know it all. I know it all.

00:55:57.262 --> 00:55:58.641
You're saved, you're saved.

00:55:58.642 --> 00:56:01.301
— You know it well. — Anyway, the birthday
broadcast like that

00:56:01.302 --> 00:56:05.341
I tried to prepare a fun birthday stream. In
a way, he was our first guest.

00:56:05.342 --> 00:56:08.241
— Right. — So, it kind of had a big meaning,
didn't it?

00:56:08.242 --> 00:56:10.701
— What did Caligo think? — He kept sending
me Shorts all day.

00:56:10.702 --> 00:56:12.102
Me?

00:56:12.182 --> 00:56:14.015
— Clips of himself? — Oh, really?

00:56:14.802 --> 00:56:16.821
— He loved it. — We know Caligo. — Laughing alone!

00:56:16.822 --> 00:56:19.301
— You're doing great, you're doing great. —
I know him, too. He…

00:56:19.302 --> 00:56:23.302
— Caligo called me. — What was that? — He
begged me to watch his Shorts.

00:56:23.502 --> 00:56:25.901
Oh, seriously. He said he was so proud.

00:56:25.902 --> 00:56:29.041
— Oh, really? — It was really too much. —
Sending clips to win you over as a fan.

00:56:29.042 --> 00:56:34.501
Yes. He said he's really happy because he got to
introduce himself in the spot he'd always dreamed of.

00:56:34.502 --> 00:56:37.861
— He was so nervous the night before, he
barely slept. — Oh. Really?

00:56:37.862 --> 00:56:41.499
— It was adorable. I said I'd watch right
away, and watched one. — It was so good.

00:56:41.500 --> 00:56:44.499
I told him, ‘Hyung, the comments are hilarious.’

00:56:44.500 --> 00:56:47.121
He said, ‘There are more besides that one…’

00:56:47.122 --> 00:56:51.282
— He came prepared. — He kept trying to show me more.

00:56:51.442 --> 00:56:54.261
— It was so cute. — Caligo, you were so cute.

00:56:54.262 --> 00:56:56.981
— He's so genuinely devoted to PLAVE. — No, enough.

00:56:56.982 --> 00:57:00.149
— He really is. — We've practiced together a
lot, really.

00:57:00.302 --> 00:57:01.702
And us again.

00:57:01.962 --> 00:57:04.301
With everything we do as PLAVE… he helps us so much.

00:57:04.302 --> 00:57:07.524
— He really does. — He's a huge help. — He
helps us a lot.

00:57:09.062 --> 00:57:12.681
— He's a good young man, a proper young man
— Caligo, you've worked hard too.

00:57:12.682 --> 00:57:14.741
— You paid him? Fine. — Hamin worked hard, too.

00:57:14.742 --> 00:57:17.409
— Thanks, thanks. — I buy him lots of good food.

00:57:18.542 --> 00:57:22.041
— Okay. — I'm sure Hamin took care of his
appearance fee properly.

00:57:22.042 --> 00:57:26.442
— Thanks. — During the stream, PLLI kept commenting…

00:57:26.602 --> 00:57:28.461
‘Isn't that Engineer Park Jongho?’

00:57:28.462 --> 00:57:31.721
Don't. Yeah, oh that was so funny

00:57:31.722 --> 00:57:33.561
— Engineer Park Jongho… — Jongho! [Laughs]

00:57:33.562 --> 00:57:37.101
— He records us. We shared a meal—delicious tacos…

00:57:37.102 --> 00:57:39.602
Oh, you've had your meal. Yes.

00:57:40.342 --> 00:57:43.231
— A meal with Engineer Park? — Why no call? — When?!

00:57:43.342 --> 00:57:45.522
It was lunchtime.

00:57:45.642 --> 00:57:47.181
I was worried you might be tired.

00:57:47.182 --> 00:57:49.042
Oh, I had some tasty tacos.

00:57:49.482 --> 00:57:53.382
— Coffee… — Mentioned our on-stream story? —
I told him.

00:57:53.482 --> 00:57:56.861
— Yes, I told him. He knows about it, too. —
Oh, I did, I did.

00:57:56.862 --> 00:57:58.981
— Does he know? — Does he watch Shorts?

00:57:58.982 --> 00:58:02.621
It'd be strange to talk about him on stream
but not tell him, so I showed him the video.

00:58:02.622 --> 00:58:04.242
On stream…

00:58:06.162 --> 00:58:07.940
Ah. You mentioned it in advance.

00:58:08.722 --> 00:58:12.262
Thank you, engineer. He…

00:58:12.842 --> 00:58:15.401
— Did he like it? — A laughing message… — He loved it!

00:58:15.402 --> 00:58:17.541
— He's such a nice person. — saying it was hilarious.

00:58:17.542 --> 00:58:21.161
— He sent me that. — He might've read every
comment on that Short.

00:58:21.162 --> 00:58:23.461
— Still in the trunk? — No, in the studio now.

00:58:23.462 --> 00:58:24.862
He came out of the trunk?

00:58:25.542 --> 00:58:27.302
Yes. I saw it all.

00:58:27.962 --> 00:58:31.062
— Oh. I see. — He's the best. Our engineer really is.

00:58:31.182 --> 00:58:32.501
— So devoted to us. — Not really.

00:58:32.502 --> 00:58:34.669
Completely sincere. Completely sincere.

00:58:34.822 --> 00:58:37.841
— Did you just happen to see him? — Ah. I,
as you might know...

00:58:37.842 --> 00:58:40.821
— I took him a signed album. — I know. — As expected!

00:58:40.822 --> 00:58:43.878
Out of nowhere, opposite? While walking down
the street

00:58:46.222 --> 00:58:47.622
Go!

00:58:50.382 --> 00:58:56.382
— So cool! — Hamin was even busier preparing
his birthday stream on tour. Give him a hand.

00:58:56.822 --> 00:58:59.061
— It's amazing. — It's amazing, really.

00:58:59.062 --> 00:59:05.062
— Right. — Everyone's busy doing things… — Flying
a drone, playing Tekken… I seriously respect that.

00:59:05.082 --> 00:59:11.082
— Right. Well. — He works so hard to give
PLLI fun content. — And Lowkey.

00:59:11.500 --> 00:59:14.221
He really deserves applause.

00:59:14.222 --> 00:59:15.622
Seriously.

00:59:16.982 --> 00:59:18.341
The best.

00:59:18.342 --> 00:59:20.262
— Thank you. — Okay.

00:59:20.862 --> 00:59:24.661
Great. Ja, the Ggun challenge came out, too.
Noah made it. Tell us the story behind it.

00:59:24.662 --> 00:59:26.062
Right? Yeah.

00:59:27.542 --> 00:59:29.202
I keep seeing it in my feed.

00:59:31.182 --> 00:59:36.422
— When Noah-hyung first came up with the
melody… — Yes, the story behind Ggun.

00:59:36.502 --> 00:59:38.901
— He immediately said… — We had to do a challenge.

00:59:38.902 --> 00:59:42.542
— Wow. You're really into this one, huh. —
He said it right away.

00:59:42.602 --> 00:59:44.101
— It's perfect. — Noah-hyung said…

00:59:44.102 --> 00:59:46.062
As soon as I'd written the lyrics…

00:59:46.322 --> 00:59:49.221
This one is. I thought, ‘This is how we should do it.’

00:59:49.222 --> 00:59:54.641
— Ah. I thought about it. — What? — You got an idea!
— It just came to me. And it couldn't be difficult.

00:59:54.642 --> 00:59:56.141
— I'm getting it. — Easy, easy.

00:59:56.142 --> 01:00:02.142
Nothing too hard or rhythmically intricate. I
watched lots of TikToks to see how people do it.

01:00:05.642 --> 01:00:08.362
So it should really catch the eye.

01:00:08.882 --> 01:00:13.382
— I really thought a lot about it and did a
lot of research. — You researched it.

01:00:13.742 --> 01:00:16.781
I hope lots of people join in. We'll see.

01:00:16.782 --> 01:00:19.241
— PLLI will do it a lot. — Yeah. A lot.

01:00:19.242 --> 01:00:25.242
— Ja, PLLI… — It's catchy and easy. I hope
lots of PLLI try it. — Awesome.

01:00:26.682 --> 01:00:29.041
— Please join in a lot. Everyone. Uh. —
One-dimensional

01:00:29.042 --> 01:00:33.499
— Great. — The members skipped a bit in the
middle. — [Quotes the lyric]

01:00:33.500 --> 01:00:39.421
You do this, then… [Demonstrates the choreography]

01:00:39.422 --> 01:00:45.201
Just a moment. There's another move here. You
lean forward with a wave, then give a wink.

01:00:45.202 --> 01:00:46.869
Was there something like that?

01:00:47.982 --> 01:00:53.982
— I did it, didn't I? — No, I mean Hamin did it. The
others skip this part and go straight to the next move.

01:00:55.122 --> 01:00:57.861
Hit it like this. Wave, wink, then go in.

01:00:57.862 --> 01:01:00.341
— Ah. Was this here? — Ah, here it is—this one.

01:01:00.342 --> 01:01:02.602
You do a wave on that lyric, right?

01:01:02.802 --> 01:01:07.999
— Ah, there was another key point there. — Yes. Thank
you. — Look. You record with your phone in front, right?

01:01:08.000 --> 01:01:10.981
— Show your face in close-up, give a wink… —
Your phone…

01:01:10.982 --> 01:01:16.421
— It's huge. — then move back. That was
intentional. — Isn't that a tablet?

01:01:16.422 --> 01:01:17.901
— See it now! — All close-up!

01:01:17.902 --> 01:01:21.341
Ja, since we're talking about it, let's have
Noah demonstrate the Ggun challenge.

01:01:21.342 --> 01:01:24.102
— Original. — Got it. Should we sing a song then?

01:01:24.342 --> 01:01:25.781
— Five, six, seven. — Sitting, too?

01:01:25.782 --> 01:01:26.961
It's meant to be done sitting.

01:01:26.962 --> 01:01:28.841
— You can! — Noah prioritizes it. — Originally…

01:01:28.842 --> 01:01:32.241
— As simple as possible. — Oh, nice.

01:01:32.242 --> 01:01:33.682
As simple as possible.

01:01:36.942 --> 01:01:42.161
[Sings for the dance challenge]

01:01:42.162 --> 01:01:48.162
[Singing]

01:01:50.282 --> 01:01:52.241
— Oh, but this is — The original is different.

01:01:52.242 --> 01:01:54.861
It's changed from your first draft, hyung. I
liked a bit in that…

01:01:54.862 --> 01:01:56.262
No. This is right.

01:01:57.102 --> 01:02:01.381
— Yes, I changed it a bit. — There was something
good, but I can't remember. You developed it further.

01:02:01.382 --> 01:02:03.993
A bit more mainstream. Made it more mainstream.

01:02:06.062 --> 01:02:08.462
— Great. — Ja, homework for PLLI. — Great.

01:02:08.722 --> 01:02:11.082
— Homework. — Homework. Again, like this.

01:02:12.102 --> 01:02:16.141
— First choreo? — First choreo! — Calling it that…

01:02:16.142 --> 01:02:17.681
— Why? — First choreo. — Is this it?

01:02:17.682 --> 01:02:19.701
— It's choreo. No fee, sadly. — Calling it choreo…

01:02:19.702 --> 01:02:21.102
Choreo, choreo.

01:02:23.882 --> 01:02:28.501
— Paid in passion. — Okay. Paid in passion.
— Yeah. Something like that.

01:02:28.502 --> 01:02:31.962
Great. Moving on from the Ggun challenge…

01:02:32.082 --> 01:02:36.562
Ja, Yejun's Starry Night radio appearance.

01:02:37.262 --> 01:02:41.041
This was really a big deal, honestly.

01:02:41.042 --> 01:02:44.501
— More appearances left? — No, it's over. — Over?

01:02:44.502 --> 01:02:47.341
— Only 3 times. — Too short. — It was only
three times.

01:02:47.342 --> 01:02:50.502
— Three times. It was good. — A shame it's over!

01:02:50.822 --> 01:02:56.061
They gave me a great opportunity. At first, I
was so nervous. I really gave myself a hard time.

01:02:56.062 --> 01:02:57.462
Oh my.

01:02:58.462 --> 01:03:01.381
— No one scolded you. — No, no one did. —
That nervous?

01:03:01.382 --> 01:03:04.301
— I scolded myself! — Gave yourself a hard
time. — Soul gone!

01:03:04.302 --> 01:03:07.662
Ah. I really, really am this sincere. Ah. Too much.

01:03:09.062 --> 01:03:13.261
A bit. I really felt it—that I'm such a
tiny, tiny alien. Seriously.

01:03:13.262 --> 01:03:17.984
— You're good. — I saw it right from the
beginning, didn't I? Right. Yes. — Good job.

01:03:18.062 --> 01:03:22.942
He seemed unhappy with how he was doing.
He'd gone in wearing a hat, then…

01:03:24.442 --> 01:03:25.842
took it off…

01:03:27.122 --> 01:03:29.621
— and during the songs, kept… — rubbing his face.

01:03:29.622 --> 01:03:35.622
It was actually pretty cold. But I was sweating
so much, my clothes were completely soaked.

01:03:37.902 --> 01:03:40.522
— Why so nervous? That bad? — What do we do?

01:03:40.622 --> 01:03:43.621
— Nerve-racking! — A drenched dumpling! —
Really? — So nervous.

01:03:43.622 --> 01:03:46.281
— So, I — Even after all those solo radio appearances?

01:03:46.282 --> 01:03:47.761
— I… — But… — It's been so long.

01:03:47.762 --> 01:03:52.081
— But that place was such an unfamiliar
environment. — The booths were different.

01:03:52.082 --> 01:03:58.082
It wasn't the studio where we did Chin Chin
before. It was somewhere else, and really big.

01:04:00.422 --> 01:04:03.261
In that unfamiliar environment, there were
people I didn't really know.

01:04:03.262 --> 01:04:05.095
It was an unfamiliar environment.

01:04:07.302 --> 01:04:10.121
— Of course you'd be nervous. — Difficult.
My first time.

01:04:10.122 --> 01:04:16.122
I sent a support message. We send those to staff on
KakaoTalk. Mine was originally much more difficult.

01:04:19.702 --> 01:04:24.999
It was long: ‘Hello, please take good care
of me today…’

01:04:25.000 --> 01:04:28.499
But the staff said, ‘Yejun is so nervous…

01:04:28.500 --> 01:04:32.121
he might make a mistake.’

01:04:32.122 --> 01:04:38.122
They thought it'd be too hard, so I
shortened it. It was originally much longer.

01:04:38.662 --> 01:04:44.662
Then Bamby joined me partway through. If he
hadn't been there, I would've cried.

01:04:45.242 --> 01:04:46.861
— Nervous, Bamby? — So close! — Content!

01:04:46.862 --> 01:04:50.918
— Crying would've made good content! — Not
nervous? — I wasn't. — Really?

01:04:50.962 --> 01:04:53.781
Maybe it's the pressure of being the main DJ.

01:04:53.782 --> 01:04:59.242
I guess I felt the pressure. But now, the
longer time passes, the better it gets.

01:04:59.342 --> 01:05:03.499
— That's the frustrating part about the very first
day. — I was nervous the whole first day. — Right away.

01:05:03.500 --> 01:05:06.999
But it got better as time passed.

01:05:07.000 --> 01:05:10.481
— And better still the next day. — It
gradually got better. Right,

01:05:10.482 --> 01:05:11.882
muscle memory

01:05:11.942 --> 01:05:17.582
It was a really valuable experience. And
everyone at Starry Night…

01:05:18.022 --> 01:05:21.221
— took such good care of me. — They took
such good care of you.

01:05:21.222 --> 01:05:23.921
— It's left behind as a good memory. Thank
you so much. — Thank you.

01:05:23.922 --> 01:05:25.461
You really did such a great job.

01:05:25.462 --> 01:05:31.462
I felt so proud, even though it wasn't me. Starry Night
is such a famous, huge show, and you hosted it, hyung.

01:05:31.562 --> 01:05:33.042
So,

01:05:35.082 --> 01:05:37.621
— Thank you! You hosted it. — Unbelievable.
— Our PLAVE leader!

01:05:37.622 --> 01:05:43.622
— No way. Seriously, no way. Leader. — MC. I
mean, I kinda felt a bit proud, you know.

01:05:44.102 --> 01:05:46.213
— No way. Seriously. — Wow. Seriously.

01:05:46.442 --> 01:05:49.242
— You really worked hard. — Can I talk about that?

01:05:49.362 --> 01:05:51.141
— Can we talk about it? — I…

01:05:51.142 --> 01:05:53.581
— What? — Can I talk about it? — Oh, that! — Go ahead.

01:05:53.582 --> 01:05:54.901
What, what.

01:05:54.902 --> 01:05:58.001
— Sure. Yeah. — [Hesitates] — Why wouldn't
you be able to talk about it? — What?

01:05:58.002 --> 01:06:00.724
— No, what is it? — Sure. — Definitely, I'm sure.

01:06:02.022 --> 01:06:04.401
— It's true, after all. — You didn't do
anything wrong!

01:06:04.402 --> 01:06:05.802
No, what is it?

01:06:06.582 --> 01:06:09.841
What is it? Come on, just talk a little. I'm
dying of frustration. Just talk to me.

01:06:09.842 --> 01:06:12.620
— Just tell us! Hurry! — Here… — Heart racing now?

01:06:12.702 --> 01:06:14.101
Weird.

01:06:14.102 --> 01:06:15.602
We went there…

01:06:16.402 --> 01:06:17.802
Can I talk about it?

01:06:18.262 --> 01:06:20.942
Park Hyo-shin sunbaenim. We said hello to him.

01:06:21.842 --> 01:06:25.009
— I'm jealous — I'm really jealous, you
know. — And also.

01:06:25.522 --> 01:06:27.921
— And I greeted Bae Chul-soo, too. — Ah,
this is really crazy

01:06:27.922 --> 01:06:31.341
‘Hello, we're PLAVE.’ That's how we
introduced ourselves.

01:06:31.342 --> 01:06:34.741
— Ah, I'm really jealous. — I'm having an
experience that doesn't even make sense.

01:06:34.742 --> 01:06:37.361
— That happened before the radio show. —
Before the show…

01:06:37.362 --> 01:06:39.541
— Nervous. — Nerve-racking! — Understandable.

01:06:39.542 --> 01:06:42.801
— Before the show, I'd seen a god! — Park
Hyo-shin! — Of course.

01:06:42.802 --> 01:06:44.202
Huge.

01:06:47.242 --> 01:06:49.702
And I'd met Bae Chul-soo.

01:06:49.742 --> 01:06:53.041
— Total legend. — So I was shaking so badly.
Seriously. Wow.

01:06:53.042 --> 01:06:55.961
— ‘I'm in trouble.’ — I started the show
already nervous…

01:06:55.962 --> 01:06:57.742
Already. Nervous.

01:06:58.622 --> 01:07:01.361
— Maxed out. — I think I got even more
nervous because of that.

01:07:01.362 --> 01:07:05.221
— I can imagine. — There's no other choice. — No
choice. — Oh, but that's true. I see what you mean.

01:07:05.222 --> 01:07:09.142
— Seriously. — You were already nervous when
you went in.

01:07:10.102 --> 01:07:12.999
— Bamby went to his concert… — He's so frustrating!

01:07:13.000 --> 01:07:15.181
— We have to discuss this, hyung. — So frustrating!

01:07:15.182 --> 01:07:16.241
Ah! A video message!

01:07:16.242 --> 01:07:18.541
— Yejun-hyung told me while we worked. Bamby… — I…

01:07:18.542 --> 01:07:20.501
If I may, I'd like to say something here.

01:07:20.502 --> 01:07:21.902
Me too.

01:07:23.822 --> 01:07:29.822
met Park Hyo-shin sunbaenim. And they talked. So the
first thing I asked was, ‘You told him about the concert…’

01:07:30.422 --> 01:07:33.202
‘right?’ He said, ‘No, he didn't.’

01:07:33.462 --> 01:07:35.761
— Bamby… — Not a single word? — I said…

01:07:35.762 --> 01:07:37.721
— His concerts and musicals. — I was shocked!

01:07:37.722 --> 01:07:41.061
— Right, we went to loads of them. — So,

01:07:41.062 --> 01:07:44.501
We saw him so many times, but Bamby didn't
mention any of it.

01:07:44.502 --> 01:07:50.482
— How?! — Just said hello. I was nervous,
too. He was right in front of us! — Exactly.

01:07:50.602 --> 01:07:53.742
Bamby was beside me, standing like this.

01:07:53.862 --> 01:07:56.529
— No. From start to finish. — It's over? Really?

01:07:57.802 --> 01:07:59.541
— He'd think you were a figurine! — Fool.

01:07:59.542 --> 01:08:01.782
Then he hid behind a wall, like this.

01:08:01.822 --> 01:08:05.862
— Really? — No. Why didn't you say anything?
When I said that.

01:08:06.002 --> 01:08:09.741
I asked why, and he said, ‘Hyung, I hate that
I'm like this, too.’ Then he just stood there.

01:08:09.742 --> 01:08:11.121
Really?

01:08:11.122 --> 01:08:12.982
Ah, but it's so cute, so cute.

01:08:14.022 --> 01:08:15.921
How could you possibly do something like that?

01:08:15.922 --> 01:08:17.421
I'm so annoyed I could die!

01:08:17.422 --> 01:08:19.562
I just can't understand it.

01:08:20.582 --> 01:08:23.401
— Ah, I'm seriously mad. Ah, why. — I'm so
mad. I'm really, really mad.

01:08:23.402 --> 01:08:29.402
If it were me, I'd say hello and wait for
Yejun-hyung to finish talking…

01:08:30.022 --> 01:08:32.941
— So, you know... that's what I'm saying. —
then jump straight in.

01:08:32.942 --> 01:08:35.142
‘Sunbaenim, I went to your concert…’

01:08:35.282 --> 01:08:41.282
‘I was so moved. If it's not too much trouble, could
I have your number?’ That's what you should've done.

01:08:44.142 --> 01:08:46.001
— Maybe he… — Eunho-hyung, you're good!

01:08:46.002 --> 01:08:52.002
— And that you'd seen his musicals. — ‘I'll
get you tickets next time.’ That could happen.

01:08:52.842 --> 01:08:55.175
Ah, were you just doing a tiny impression?

01:08:55.822 --> 01:08:58.741
‘I'll invite you next time.’ That's how it goes.

01:08:58.742 --> 01:09:00.661
— An impression out of nowhere! — From the side…

01:09:00.662 --> 01:09:04.261
— Ugh, I'm so frustrated, seriously. I
should have gone. Ah. — Ah, but.

01:09:04.262 --> 01:09:06.701
— But... Ah, but... — Bamby got to go. I
should've gone.

01:09:06.702 --> 01:09:09.801
— In Bamby's defense… — Speak up for me! — Bamby…

01:09:09.802 --> 01:09:12.041
Not that atmosphere at all. We'd just seen a god!

01:09:12.042 --> 01:09:15.061
— Ah, really? — I don't think Noah-hyung
could've done it, either. — A god…

01:09:15.062 --> 01:09:18.761
— We'd seen one. — But. But you could've
said how much you love him.

01:09:18.762 --> 01:09:20.501
— You should've said it! — You should've!

01:09:20.502 --> 01:09:23.621
Noah-hyung, when you get tense, your nose turns red.

01:09:23.622 --> 01:09:26.281
So the truth will come out even more, right?

01:09:26.282 --> 01:09:28.421
— Noah-hyung's nervous nose is red, like
Rudolph. — No…

01:09:28.422 --> 01:09:32.662
— My nose, around my mouth, and my ears all
go red. — Really? — Ah, really?

01:09:32.882 --> 01:09:37.641
— Oh, something like that exists. — Ah, seriously me. —
I hated myself for not being able to say a single word.

01:09:37.642 --> 01:09:40.661
— Another chance, you'll meet again, right?
— Seriously…

01:09:40.662 --> 01:09:45.001
— I really hated it. Seriously. — His
silhouette was hilarious. He was like this.

01:09:45.002 --> 01:09:49.542
All that love… It was written all over his face.

01:09:50.222 --> 01:09:52.741
— His love… — Feelings written on his face!

01:09:52.742 --> 01:09:56.181
— His whole body showed it! — Really? I didn't know!

01:09:56.182 --> 01:09:58.322
You really were standing like this.

01:09:59.282 --> 01:10:00.741
— So frustrating! — Seriously!

01:10:00.742 --> 01:10:03.242
Did you go home and reflect on it? Regret it?

01:10:03.322 --> 01:10:07.561
— Forget reflecting. I actually hit myself. Seriously.
— You actually did? — Ah, why are you like this?

01:10:07.562 --> 01:10:11.021
— Hello? — Ah, but the staff members who
were there at the time too.

01:10:11.022 --> 01:10:15.441
— ‘Bamby, why aren't you saying anything?’ —
I just can't understand it.

01:10:15.442 --> 01:10:19.121
— I'm frustrated on your behalf! — I don't
know. Just... — But if I get another chance…

01:10:19.122 --> 01:10:21.981
— Next time, definitely! — You've met before
now. — Definitely.

01:10:21.982 --> 01:10:24.501
— I won't do anything I'll regret. Yeah. —
Yeah. — Uh. I...

01:10:24.502 --> 01:10:26.521
— How?! — Ja, then, ja. Let's practice!

01:10:26.522 --> 01:10:28.561
— What do I do? — Ja, I'm sunbaenim. — I'm good!

01:10:28.562 --> 01:10:29.941
With us, he'll even roll around.

01:10:29.942 --> 01:10:33.581
— Got it all done. All done, right here. Well,
how... um... — You should practice, though.

01:10:33.582 --> 01:10:36.382
— Huh? Hello? — Hello. Hello, sir.

01:10:36.582 --> 01:10:40.415
— Huh. Yeah, hello. — I really enjoyed your
musical and your concert.

01:10:40.462 --> 01:10:41.862
Excuse me, but who...

01:10:43.282 --> 01:10:46.541
— Bamby — Yeah. — PLAVE — Ah Bamby-ssi, oh
yes, nice to meet you

01:10:46.542 --> 01:10:48.182
Thank you.

01:10:50.282 --> 01:10:52.681
— No good! — What are you doing? — Keep talking!

01:10:52.682 --> 01:10:55.181
— This won't do! — What? — Why didn't you ask there?

01:10:55.182 --> 01:10:57.161
— What else do I say? — Ask for his number!

01:10:57.162 --> 01:11:00.241
You should go, ‘Sunbaenim, could I have a hug?’

01:11:00.242 --> 01:11:02.261
Jaejoong sunbaenim: two hugs! Ja, Noah! — Crazy!

01:11:02.262 --> 01:11:05.421
Asking for a number on your first meeting?
Inappropriate!

01:11:05.422 --> 01:11:07.921
Ja, ja. Watch! — He hugged me twice. — Look!

01:11:07.922 --> 01:11:11.866
— I hate it! — First meeting! — Look, I'm
telling you. — Ja, like this…

01:11:13.982 --> 01:11:18.704
— Oh. This is overkill. — I am. I am. — I
wouldn't like it if someone did that to me.

01:11:18.742 --> 01:11:20.981
— Really! — I thought I'd become a ghost!

01:11:20.982 --> 01:11:24.301
Right. I looked at something I shouldn't
have. I'm kind of like this, you know.

01:11:24.302 --> 01:11:26.469
Ja, let's try again. Ja, ready, action.

01:11:28.942 --> 01:11:30.386
Really. This much is fine.

01:11:30.702 --> 01:11:33.091
— This much is fine. — I'm Noah from PLAVE.

01:11:33.162 --> 01:11:35.662
— Noah-ssi, nice to meet you. — Heard of us?

01:11:35.862 --> 01:11:38.981
— Of course I know you. — Oh, really? How do
you know us?

01:11:38.982 --> 01:11:41.201
Ah PLAVE they're super famous, aren't they?

01:11:41.202 --> 01:11:45.261
I'm such a fan. I've been to your concerts and
musicals. I saw your show at Munhak recently, too.

01:11:45.262 --> 01:11:47.382
— But. — Oh, really? — That's nice.

01:11:47.942 --> 01:11:51.441
— Oh really? Back when it was that cold —
Oh, I'm really, really a fan. Seriously.

01:11:51.442 --> 01:11:54.382
— Oh, really? Oh, thank you so much. — Thank you.

01:11:57.802 --> 01:12:00.021
— I jump straight in. — I… — This much is fine.

01:12:00.022 --> 01:12:03.021
— You're diving straight in, huh? — Yeah,
I'm really going in right away.

01:12:03.022 --> 01:12:06.161
— I'd go straight for his number. — Ja,
Eunho's turn. — Too much!

01:12:06.162 --> 01:12:08.521
— I really do it. — Be honest. Show us the real thing.

01:12:08.522 --> 01:12:11.241
I always do it. Even when I go on the radio.

01:12:11.242 --> 01:12:13.641
— But… — I got Hanhae sunbaenim's number, too.

01:12:13.642 --> 01:12:18.741
Before we do it. You can tell just by looking into
their eyes—whether they're going to give it or not.

01:12:18.742 --> 01:12:21.221
— I'll ask anyway. — Even if they seem unwilling?

01:12:21.222 --> 01:12:23.701
This isn't rude, right? Honestly. Contact
info. Contact info.

01:12:23.702 --> 01:12:26.901
— No. It's rude. From my perspective. — No,
asking isn't rude, is it?

01:12:26.902 --> 01:12:28.661
— It could be awkward. — Or rude. — Awkward!

01:12:28.662 --> 01:12:32.142
No, you can just say sorry when the rejection happens.

01:12:32.362 --> 01:12:34.661
— What… — Why do something you'd apologize for?

01:12:34.662 --> 01:12:40.082
— What? — That's how I see it. — Ja, let's
watch and judge whether it's rude or not. — Why?

01:12:40.782 --> 01:12:42.182
Go ahead and try it.

01:12:42.342 --> 01:12:43.742
Hello, sunbaenim.

01:12:44.142 --> 01:12:50.142
I'm such a huge fan. I went to Munhak and your musicals.
Since I was little, I've sung your songs at karaoke…

01:12:55.782 --> 01:12:58.001
— I love your Gift album, sunbaenim! — I have to go.

01:12:58.002 --> 01:12:59.402
Ah, yes, I understand.

01:13:01.782 --> 01:13:04.221
I sing Memories Resemble Love so much…

01:13:04.222 --> 01:13:06.862
— Thank you. — I raise it two keys…

01:13:07.882 --> 01:13:10.221
or down a key if my throat's bad. At Su Karaoke…

01:13:10.222 --> 01:13:12.821
This isn't a fan meeting.

01:13:12.822 --> 01:13:16.081
— So often at karaoke! — Thank you. — He can't leave…

01:13:16.082 --> 01:13:21.141
— He needs to get past you… — Meeting you like this after
my debut… I finally feel… — You're blocking his way…

01:13:21.142 --> 01:13:24.781
— like I've become a singer. — He keeps
blocking him so he can't leave! — A singer…

01:13:24.782 --> 01:13:27.560
— Blocking. — Becoming a singer feels so real now.

01:13:27.602 --> 01:13:30.341
— If it's not too much trouble, your number?
— Thank you.

01:13:30.342 --> 01:13:32.342
May I ask? Because I really...

01:13:32.662 --> 01:13:35.141
So much to ask about singing. So much I want to learn!

01:13:35.142 --> 01:13:40.309
— Yes, but I have somewhere to be… — There's so
much I want to learn. But first, your number…

01:13:41.422 --> 01:13:42.882
Okay, well... Ah...

01:13:42.982 --> 01:13:46.181
Sorry, Manager. If it's inconvenient, I
can't help that…

01:13:46.182 --> 01:13:50.221
— Keep at it until it works! — An eager
junior singer… Your number?

01:13:50.222 --> 01:13:51.622
Ah, next...

01:13:51.882 --> 01:13:54.101
— Next time. — Move aside! — I'll say hello then…

01:13:54.102 --> 01:13:55.502
Ah, done.

01:13:57.422 --> 01:13:59.382
Oh, now he's in sad mode.

01:13:59.762 --> 01:14:03.095
— I'll see you next time. Take care. — Now
he's in sad mode!

01:14:03.182 --> 01:14:06.861
— Ah, so that's how you do it, huh? — Now...
Ah... Uh... — Yes. Like this. I go in like this.

01:14:06.862 --> 01:14:09.601
— Good! — They can't help but hear you out.

01:14:09.602 --> 01:14:12.681
Once you cross that line, you go beyond just
expressing your feelings…

01:14:12.682 --> 01:14:14.515
What do you mean, cross the line?

01:14:17.582 --> 01:14:20.961
— Ah, but ah... — That's how you do it. You
need a thick skin.

01:14:20.962 --> 01:14:22.701
— But… — Just jump in like that!

01:14:22.702 --> 01:14:26.061
— Without introducing yourself? — Number first!

01:14:26.062 --> 01:14:29.322
After that. If he asks first, I'll introduce
myself then.

01:14:29.902 --> 01:14:35.181
— No introduction? — If he asks, ‘Who are
you?’: ‘I'm Eunho from PLAVE.’ — Later!

01:14:35.182 --> 01:14:38.281
— But who are you? — Ah, ah that time —
because I have too much to say

01:14:38.282 --> 01:14:41.361
Do you assume he'll recognize you first?

01:14:41.362 --> 01:14:45.861
— No, Just. — You're just in a hurry to get
your point across. — It's what you do.

01:14:45.862 --> 01:14:48.422
— Ah, that's... — Right. Like this. No.

01:14:49.582 --> 01:14:53.321
He'd assume I'm in entertainment. We're
meeting at the radio station, after all.

01:14:53.322 --> 01:14:55.766
Since you'd be meeting at the radio station.

01:14:57.782 --> 01:14:59.421
— He'd know I'm a junior. — Then!

01:14:59.422 --> 01:15:03.761
Park Hyo-shin sunbaenim's expression…

01:15:03.762 --> 01:15:09.461
He didn't look like he wanted to get away.
He seemed really friendly.

01:15:09.462 --> 01:15:15.462
— Thank you! — We both waited for the other to
speak. A long pause! I should've spoken then.

01:15:20.782 --> 01:15:23.342
In the end, this is how it turned out...

01:15:23.942 --> 01:15:26.082
So I was really frustrated back then.

01:15:26.182 --> 01:15:28.902
We used up a lifetime's worth of luck.

01:15:29.442 --> 01:15:32.362
That's why I couldn't help but get so nervous.

01:15:32.962 --> 01:15:35.182
He's a celebrity's celebrity.

01:15:37.002 --> 01:15:40.502
But because I know Bamby is just naturally
that kind of person.

01:15:40.562 --> 01:15:41.661
— Argh! — Should've gone!

01:15:41.662 --> 01:15:43.981
I won't do that again. I've had the experience now.

01:15:43.982 --> 01:15:49.982
Next, what? Next time we're at a station, for radio
or other appearances, if we meet singers we love…

01:15:54.062 --> 01:15:57.061
Now. or admire, let's make sure we tell them.

01:15:57.062 --> 01:15:59.401
No more mistakes like this anymore.

01:15:59.402 --> 01:16:02.022
— Great. — I promise, PLLI.

01:16:02.822 --> 01:16:06.301
— It's not really a mistake. Just a missed
opportunity. — Ah, it's not a mistake, is it?

01:16:06.302 --> 01:16:09.421
— Okay. Just a little incident, with some
regrets. — Just a little incident.

01:16:09.422 --> 01:16:12.499
— Everyone gets nervous. — He won't speak
next time, either! — Again?

01:16:12.500 --> 01:16:14.999
— A member must help. — Go together. — I'll
do it if I'm there.

01:16:15.000 --> 01:16:17.741
— Yejun should've helped him speak. — Go with someone!

01:16:17.742 --> 01:16:21.262
— Straight for the number! — You couldn't
say it either.

01:16:21.422 --> 01:16:25.441
— Okay, not that—next, next You were just as
nervous, hyung. — Just as nervous!

01:16:25.442 --> 01:16:29.041
— I'll speak. — How was it? — You gave the
album, hyung. Not much talk!

01:16:29.042 --> 01:16:30.442
How was it, how was it?

01:16:35.122 --> 01:16:37.341
— How? — Said hello. — Don't gang up! — Hello.

01:16:37.342 --> 01:16:39.941
— Oh, teacher, so so — Why?

01:16:39.942 --> 01:16:42.061
— What, hyung? — Dragging him down! — Me, too…

01:16:42.062 --> 01:16:43.501
— I go blank. — All nervous.

01:16:43.502 --> 01:16:46.161
— Gave the album… — Really? — I was shaking!

01:16:46.162 --> 01:16:47.361
I don't remember.

01:16:47.362 --> 01:16:50.195
— So what didn't we talk about then? — No, because.

01:16:50.382 --> 01:16:52.661
— Didn't know he was there. — Unexpected!

01:16:52.662 --> 01:16:58.021
— We found out there. Next time, we'll be
braver and speak up. — We found out there!

01:16:58.022 --> 01:16:59.800
You want to do the album, right?

01:17:00.362 --> 01:17:02.921
— Understood! Fighting! — Park Hyo-shin
sunbaenim, fighting!

01:17:02.922 --> 01:17:05.861
We love you, sunbaenim. If I meet you someday…

01:17:05.862 --> 01:17:10.582
— That was a good path. — I really want to
ask you for your contact info.

01:17:10.702 --> 01:17:13.101
If this reaches you: we were the two who
said hello that day.

01:17:13.102 --> 01:17:14.502
Really, sunbaenim.

01:17:15.382 --> 01:17:19.549
— Thank you. — I'll say hello once more. —
Sunbaenim, I'd love to meet you.

01:17:19.562 --> 01:17:22.229
I'll sing all of Memories Resemble Love for you…

01:17:22.762 --> 01:17:24.781
— Two keys higher! Got it. — Okay. — Understood.

01:17:24.782 --> 01:17:28.521
— Enough ‘resembling love’! — Let's go. —
Ja, Eunho bought 18 liters of cooking oil.

01:17:28.522 --> 01:17:31.021
— Eighteen liters! — He goes big. — There's a reason…

01:17:31.022 --> 01:17:33.262
Oh, are you having a drink before bed?

01:17:34.642 --> 01:17:38.282
— So that you sleep well now — You're not doing shots…

01:17:38.442 --> 01:17:42.961
— of cooking oil, are you? — Oh no, I bought
it for the vibe. The vibe.

01:17:42.962 --> 01:17:48.962
— For the aesthetic? — So, — Like a restaurant… —
Right. I love that rugged-looking tin. — [Trails off]

01:17:50.442 --> 01:17:52.181
I just love that kind of vibe so much.

01:17:52.182 --> 01:17:56.401
Is the 18-liter one the one I'm thinking of?
At that store? Yeah, that's it. Right here.

01:17:56.402 --> 01:17:58.846
— The square one. That one! — The metal tin?

01:17:59.302 --> 01:18:01.801
— Why? — The oil will spoil quickly. — So much oil!

01:18:01.802 --> 01:18:06.341
I also bought a deep fryer.

01:18:06.342 --> 01:18:08.902
— To fry food? — Yes, for the fryer.

01:18:09.182 --> 01:18:11.501
— You bought a fryer? — Yes, like this.

01:18:11.502 --> 01:18:15.335
— Did you buy Haepyo oil? Like this? Yeah. —
Yeah. I took that photo.

01:18:15.562 --> 01:18:16.962
It's the one I took.

01:18:17.142 --> 01:18:18.341
Oh, you're right.

01:18:18.342 --> 01:18:21.461
— It shows up on Google. — Uh, when you do
it... — Oh, it looks really robotic.

01:18:21.462 --> 01:18:25.518
— Bubble shows up on Google? — Uh, Eunho is
showing up — This is amazing.

01:18:26.102 --> 01:18:32.102
It's got that aesthetic. It's really heavy to pour.
You get a workout, too. You'd like that, hyung.

01:18:34.342 --> 01:18:36.561
Seriously, do it like this. Hold it like this.

01:18:36.562 --> 01:18:37.962
Then pour it like this.

01:18:38.442 --> 01:18:39.941
— 18 liters… — Vibes! — Too much!

01:18:39.942 --> 01:18:42.141
— A deadlift. — Yes, lift it like this!

01:18:42.142 --> 01:18:43.586
Be careful with your back.

01:18:44.562 --> 01:18:46.442
Anyway… That...

01:18:46.822 --> 01:18:52.081
I opened the lid the wrong way again. You know, the
rubber ring that's supposed to be like this, right?

01:18:52.082 --> 01:18:55.122
Like this. The lid you twist off.

01:18:55.542 --> 01:19:01.202
The handle broke. So I cut it out with a utility
knife and cleaned up the edges like this.

01:19:01.742 --> 01:19:04.622
— Unique! — Barely managed. — Fryer capacity?

01:19:05.002 --> 01:19:08.801
Still, it holds over one liter each time.

01:19:08.802 --> 01:19:10.469
So we can do it 18 times then.

01:19:10.702 --> 01:19:13.861
It seems like it can hold one liter. 18 times?

01:19:13.862 --> 01:19:15.441
Throw the oil away after one use?

01:19:15.442 --> 01:19:17.921
I still think I can use it about three times.

01:19:17.922 --> 01:19:20.661
— Recycling — But. — Oh, you're frying stuff now too?

01:19:20.662 --> 01:19:23.401
Frying. I'll make some for you. It tastes different!

01:19:23.402 --> 01:19:26.122
What about the fried food itself? Do you buy it?

01:19:26.482 --> 01:19:29.761
— What? — Fried food. — Sometimes homemade…
— Flour and all?

01:19:29.762 --> 01:19:32.781
— Yourself? — Sometimes I coat it with
pancake mix and flour.

01:19:32.782 --> 01:19:35.021
— Isn't that a meal kit? — That, too? — You made this?

01:19:35.022 --> 01:19:37.961
— That's a meal kit. — You made it? —
Restaurant quality!

01:19:37.962 --> 01:19:39.661
— You scared me! — Meal kit. — What a shock!

01:19:39.662 --> 01:19:43.041
Ah, it's not a meal kit. It's the fried stuff.

01:19:43.042 --> 01:19:44.101
Hey!

01:19:44.102 --> 01:19:46.421
— Pre-battered… — Frozen gim-mari seaweed rolls.

01:19:46.422 --> 01:19:49.261
— Frozen gim-mari. — Something like that kind of feel.

01:19:49.262 --> 01:19:53.002
So it's completely different. If you cook it in oil.

01:19:53.202 --> 01:19:55.701
It tastes totally different from an air
fryer. Night and day!

01:19:55.702 --> 01:19:58.101
— Totally different! — Really? — He's
serious about this.

01:19:58.102 --> 01:20:02.541
— Oh, I have something my mom used to say. There's no
food that doesn't taste good when it meets oil. — What?

01:20:02.542 --> 01:20:04.201
Frying makes everything taste good.

01:20:04.202 --> 01:20:07.021
— Ah, hold on, hold on. — Wow, even this
kind of thing again?

01:20:07.022 --> 01:20:08.261
— Me, me, me… — Amazing!

01:20:08.262 --> 01:20:10.221
I'll pack lunch for you. Please just eat it!

01:20:10.222 --> 01:20:13.101
— Ah, I don't want to, I won't eat it. — Oh
really? It's warm.

01:20:13.102 --> 01:20:17.641
— I bought Action Mask and Buriburizaemon lunchboxes.
I need to use them. — Let Action Mask try it first.

01:20:17.642 --> 01:20:19.086
I have to put them to use.

01:20:19.402 --> 01:20:20.961
— [Laughs] — Why did you buy that?

01:20:20.962 --> 01:20:23.601
— Why is he acting like that? Seriously — So cute.

01:20:23.602 --> 01:20:27.941
— Buriburizaemon. — Oh, it's cute, that thing — Thinking
maybe I'll have to pack a lunch for someone someday.

01:20:27.942 --> 01:20:30.862
— Is the fryer big? — Pretty big. — Lunchbox

01:20:32.142 --> 01:20:34.661
— Too big to move? — You can move it. It's
not that big.

01:20:34.662 --> 01:20:36.062
Oh, really?

01:20:37.282 --> 01:20:39.461
— That won't do either. — I'll pack you
lunch sometime.

01:20:39.462 --> 01:20:42.061
I'm curious, I really want to try a taste first.

01:20:42.062 --> 01:20:43.981
— I'll let you try it next time. — Okay! — Great.

01:20:43.982 --> 01:20:45.941
— Never met an 18-liter buyer. — What else?

01:20:45.942 --> 01:20:51.942
Pretty plates and presentation, it says
here. I love buying plates. Recently…

01:20:54.062 --> 01:20:57.781
Plates. I think I've probably spent around
500,000 won just on plates and bowls.

01:20:57.782 --> 01:21:00.041
— Really? Yeah. — You're saying that? — Yes. Recently.

01:21:00.042 --> 01:21:01.821
— Listen! — Bowls and tableware.

01:21:01.822 --> 01:21:03.541
A plate can cost over 100,000 won!

01:21:03.542 --> 01:21:06.061
— No, it's not that it's expensive. — Really? Yeah.

01:21:06.062 --> 01:21:08.801
Some are expensive. I bought lots. They're
so pretty; I love them.

01:21:08.802 --> 01:21:10.202
You bought loads, then.

01:21:11.882 --> 01:21:14.141
— Buriburizaemon plates? — Buriburizaemon?

01:21:14.142 --> 01:21:20.142
— Running a business? — That's the lunchbox.
— Different moods need different plating.

01:21:20.842 --> 01:21:24.681
— So… — Ah, it depends on the food... Yeah,
that's right. The right clothes.

01:21:24.682 --> 01:21:29.581
— Different moods need different plating. Do you
guys like collecting plates? — Various things.

01:21:29.582 --> 01:21:35.582
— Hamin does. — Oh, Hamin does. — No, not right
now. But when I really start decorating my place…

01:21:37.862 --> 01:21:40.462
I might buy some.

01:21:41.942 --> 01:21:44.301
Bamby, you're really into them! You love them.

01:21:44.302 --> 01:21:47.941
Is it that obvious? I do like them. I even
have a favorite brand.

01:21:47.942 --> 01:21:49.362
Oh, really?

01:21:50.442 --> 01:21:52.741
— I have it. — I'm almost all Daiso.

01:21:52.742 --> 01:21:58.321
— No Ichiran bowl yet. — I like plain. — Daiso's white
bowls cost 2–3,000 won. Bigger ones… — The dishes?

01:21:58.322 --> 01:21:59.722
Oh, plain, plain.

01:22:00.062 --> 01:22:05.481
— But... — Five thousand, maybe? — Even just
eating snacks… The way you plate them…

01:22:05.482 --> 01:22:09.841
— It's different. — It makes me happy.
Putting snacks on a pretty plate…

01:22:09.842 --> 01:22:12.661
— Right, lots of people are like that. —
That's important.

01:22:12.662 --> 01:22:15.601
— Don't you just eat snacks out of the bag?
— Something like that...

01:22:15.602 --> 01:22:19.421
— Completely different. — Keep moving this stuff
onto the plate, eat from it, then wash the dishes?

01:22:19.422 --> 01:22:21.781
— Enjoy life a little, hyung! — Exactly.

01:22:21.782 --> 01:22:25.161
— So, you know, stuff like that, ramen
too... — Ah. You know, something like that.

01:22:25.162 --> 01:22:28.321
— Ichiran's bowl adds atmosphere and flavor.
— Exactly.

01:22:28.322 --> 01:22:30.541
— We bought one. — I couldn't. — Oh, right.

01:22:30.542 --> 01:22:33.061
Plastic just doesn't give the same taste!

01:22:33.062 --> 01:22:36.621
So that's the feeling, you know—Pyongyang
cold noodles too, that...

01:22:36.622 --> 01:22:39.542
— The metal bowl! — Metal! — That sort of thing.

01:22:39.722 --> 01:22:42.382
No, I mean. Say you bought Ichiran ramen.

01:22:42.602 --> 01:22:44.435
But then there's no bowl, though.

01:22:44.662 --> 01:22:47.622
Of course you'd use a bowl. But if it's cup noodles…

01:22:47.882 --> 01:22:49.481
— Why transfer cup noodles? — Just eat!

01:22:49.482 --> 01:22:55.482
— That vibe! — For snacks, reach in the bag,
eat, then fold and tie it shut.

01:22:55.942 --> 01:22:57.801
— Can eat that way. — Sure, hyung.

01:22:57.802 --> 01:23:00.821
— Nothing wrong with it. — But there's
something new to it.

01:23:00.822 --> 01:23:03.981
— That is, — It's treating yourself by using
a pretty dish.

01:23:03.982 --> 01:23:08.701
— Yeah... Uh, are you not in a good mood? — Something
like at the end of the day, a little... — That is,

01:23:08.702 --> 01:23:11.021
— Well... — You can put snacks on a different plate…

01:23:11.022 --> 01:23:12.633
and eat them that way, right?

01:23:13.382 --> 01:23:14.782
Why couldn't you?

01:23:15.982 --> 01:23:18.093
Okay, so that's how you're playing it.

01:23:18.482 --> 01:23:20.371
— Of course you can. — Good, okay.

01:23:20.902 --> 01:23:24.361
— Like sake: you pour it into a special cup.

01:23:24.362 --> 01:23:26.621
Yeah. That's right. Ah... um...

01:23:26.622 --> 01:23:27.881
— That vibe! — So different!

01:23:27.882 --> 01:23:31.461
— Ah... Uh, right, — There's some vibe to
it. — No, I'm just lazy to do the dishes.

01:23:31.462 --> 01:23:34.481
— Yes, washing up is a real hassle. — The
dishes are Bamby-hyung's job, right?

01:23:34.482 --> 01:23:37.681
— I see. — That's fine. I don't have many.

01:23:37.682 --> 01:23:39.082
[Brief interjection]

01:23:39.882 --> 01:23:43.302
— two favorites. Plates and… — Plates. — Only two?

01:23:43.462 --> 01:23:44.862
Spoon or...

01:23:45.122 --> 01:23:46.542
Two and that cup too.

01:23:46.902 --> 01:23:50.180
— Two favorites out of how many? — The ones
I saw recently…

01:23:50.902 --> 01:23:53.182
— This cup or this cup? — Wine?

01:23:53.362 --> 01:23:55.781
— Wine glasses? Haven't seen them. — Glasses.

01:23:55.782 --> 01:23:57.101
What color is this...

01:23:57.102 --> 01:24:01.702
— Is it gradient? — I have some silver ones,
and some ceramic plates.

01:24:02.462 --> 01:24:04.381
— If you know, you know. — Hamin's seen it?

01:24:04.382 --> 01:24:06.641
— Hamin's seen everything. — I remember. — You have?

01:24:06.642 --> 01:24:09.142
Every time I visit, there's something new.

01:24:09.422 --> 01:24:11.681
So you research them before buying.

01:24:11.682 --> 01:24:13.161
Look it up and then buy it...

01:24:13.162 --> 01:24:16.561
Oh, just passing by, I notice it when I
happen to see it somewhere

01:24:16.562 --> 01:24:19.721
By chance. You don't specifically go out to buy them.

01:24:19.722 --> 01:24:24.555
I don't go out of my way, but if I happen to
pass by and see it, I'd definitely buy it.

01:24:26.662 --> 01:24:30.061
— Right. — Ja, 18 liters of oil brought us here!

01:24:30.062 --> 01:24:31.462
End.

01:24:31.500 --> 01:24:36.981
Ja, everyone. Did you realize 2026 is nearly
over already?

01:24:36.982 --> 01:24:38.382
It's nearly over.

01:24:39.782 --> 01:24:42.021
— January… — Do you remember January? — Of course.

01:24:42.022 --> 01:24:44.241
— January 2026… I don't remember it.

01:24:44.242 --> 01:24:45.361
What did we do in January?

01:24:45.362 --> 01:24:48.981
— Oh. I don't remember well. — Don't remember?
Not at all. I feel like it was just yesterday.

01:24:48.982 --> 01:24:51.821
— Time flies! — What happened in January?

01:24:51.822 --> 01:24:54.861
— We said ‘Happy New Year.’ — Right, in
2026. — We did.

01:24:54.862 --> 01:24:59.942
2026. 2026. No, what was the biggest thing
in January 2026?

01:25:00.402 --> 01:25:02.958
— We had our… — Born Savage, right? — Gocheok.

01:25:04.462 --> 01:25:06.021
— Gocheok. — Born Savage, too?

01:25:06.022 --> 01:25:08.241
— Not Gocheok? — February? — February. — Was it?

01:25:08.242 --> 01:25:11.181
— Oh, it was February? — Born Savage was
February. — It was February?

01:25:11.182 --> 01:25:13.515
Gocheok concert was in January, wasn't it?

01:25:14.822 --> 01:25:16.222
It had to be January.

01:25:17.222 --> 01:25:18.622
It's March?

01:25:19.762 --> 01:25:22.762
What big thing happened in January?

01:25:23.982 --> 01:25:25.221
— I forget. — Gocheok? November?

01:25:25.222 --> 01:25:27.201
— Apparently November. — November?! — Really?

01:25:27.202 --> 01:25:29.421
— A year already? — I can't remember. — It
was November.

01:25:29.422 --> 01:25:31.921
— No way! It's been a year since Gocheok?!

01:25:31.922 --> 01:25:34.700
No way, we didn't do the encore concert this year?

01:25:34.762 --> 01:25:38.095
— Didn't do it. Didn't do it. — Ah, we
didn't do the encore?

01:25:38.702 --> 01:25:40.102
Really?

01:25:40.982 --> 01:25:42.760
— Ah. Really? — But? At Gocheok?

01:25:42.822 --> 01:25:44.101
That was last year.

01:25:44.102 --> 01:25:45.801
— November encore? — Yes. What's that?

01:25:45.802 --> 01:25:50.122
Ah. That thing. What is that? Did we all do
it live? New Year's tarot?

01:25:51.362 --> 01:25:53.221
— Remember? — Tarot! — Oh, that!

01:25:53.222 --> 01:25:55.821
— Unforgettable tarot. — A legendary stream!
— Oh, that!

01:25:55.822 --> 01:25:58.501
— I'll never forget the tarot reading. — Oh, tarot.

01:25:58.502 --> 01:26:03.242
— That's January, right? — The tarot stream?
— Tarot! I remember that vividly.

01:26:03.402 --> 01:26:05.781
— That tarot reading… — Why, why Eunho-ssi?

01:26:05.782 --> 01:26:11.621
— The tarot stream? — It was so memorable. The
reading was so accurate. — It looked weird, huh?

01:26:11.622 --> 01:26:13.022
Why, why?

01:26:15.562 --> 01:26:18.902
The tarot stream feels like two or three
years ago to me.

01:26:19.082 --> 01:26:21.693
Oh, really? Ah, that feels kind of old, though.

01:26:22.022 --> 01:26:23.281
Prof. Hamin's ‘You Can Do It.’

01:26:23.282 --> 01:26:24.782
So much has happened, huh.

01:26:26.122 --> 01:26:27.941
— Our solo streams, right? — Solo streams.

01:26:27.942 --> 01:26:30.561
— Solo streams! Professor concept. — Fun!

01:26:30.562 --> 01:26:36.173
— Ah, so this is how we did it. — It's been a while
since I got banned from PUBG live on stream, too.

01:26:36.942 --> 01:26:39.241
Ah, I see. That's great.

01:26:39.242 --> 01:26:41.741
Oh, the Caligo Pt.2 comeback stream…

01:26:41.742 --> 01:26:44.662
March or April, right? March. Ah. April. April.

01:26:45.322 --> 01:26:50.161
— We streamed so much! — We worked hard
recording Caligo Pt.2 in February.

01:26:50.162 --> 01:26:53.801
— Ah. That's why it feels so old. — Back
then, we did it during the holiday, remember?

01:26:53.802 --> 01:26:55.635
Yeah. That's right. That's right.

01:26:57.000 --> 01:26:58.500
Oh, I see.

01:26:59.222 --> 01:27:01.761
— We did a lot, didn't we? — We really did a lot.

01:27:01.762 --> 01:27:05.901
We actually did a lot of broadcasts like this,
and honestly, we did a lot of albums too.

01:27:05.902 --> 01:27:08.981
— So, — Ready. Still, we really lived hard,
going on tour this year too.

01:27:08.982 --> 01:27:10.760
We really lived hard, didn't we.

01:27:11.542 --> 01:27:13.461
— Remember… — What else? We did so much.

01:27:13.462 --> 01:27:16.851
— The YouTube concert in Japan, too. — We
even went to Japan.

01:27:16.942 --> 01:27:18.981
— Remember? — Yes, lots. — TMA, too!

01:27:18.982 --> 01:27:21.593
— 5 songs... 5 songs, right? — Right, TMA, too.

01:27:22.322 --> 01:27:23.722
I really did a lot.

01:27:24.462 --> 01:27:26.581
— So much! — OSTs, too. — Lots of OSTs.

01:27:26.582 --> 01:27:28.082
OST, that's right.

01:27:28.582 --> 01:27:31.881
— It turned out that way. And the milet collab.

01:27:31.882 --> 01:27:35.493
— Oh. Right. From Japan, a bit. — Right, the
milet collaboration.

01:27:36.742 --> 01:27:39.182
— Another collab's coming. — Back again!

01:27:39.702 --> 01:27:40.941
— We did a lot! — Once.

01:27:40.942 --> 01:27:43.502
It just ended up working out like this.

01:27:45.062 --> 01:27:47.741
— Make the most of each day. — Lovely thought.

01:27:47.742 --> 01:27:49.142
I love it so much

01:27:49.782 --> 01:27:51.182
— GS Bread. — GS Bread

01:27:51.942 --> 01:27:55.021
— Ah, that colored bread — PLLI really loved
those this year, too. — That.

01:27:55.022 --> 01:27:57.521
— Bread, too! — Pepero came first. — Yes, Pepero.

01:27:57.522 --> 01:28:00.021
— Our bread's in my freezer. — Pepero was last year.

01:28:00.022 --> 01:28:04.141
— Our bread's still in my freezer. — Pepero
was last year. — I bought about 20 at GS25.

01:28:04.142 --> 01:28:06.761
— Excuse me? — Still have it... — What are
you talking about?

01:28:06.762 --> 01:28:09.341
Ah. I still have that GS bread in the freezer.

01:28:09.342 --> 01:28:11.981
— Ah, the freezer? — I bought 20 of them back then.

01:28:11.982 --> 01:28:16.561
— Through B Mart. — Ah, that thing— you know, that
thing — That thing, are you gonna deep-fry it later?

01:28:16.562 --> 01:28:19.141
— Could you fry it? Sounds good! — You
could! — Delicious!

01:28:19.142 --> 01:28:23.401
— Thank you… — Fried... fried bread. — Nice.
— Thanks for telling me how to use it up.

01:28:23.402 --> 01:28:28.101
— Great. — Great. Ja, everyone. Apparently Pepero
was two years ago! It wasn't last year? — Yes. Ja.

01:28:28.102 --> 01:28:31.301
— Ah. Two years ago? Really? — Really? —
Wasn't it last year? It's two years ago.

01:28:31.302 --> 01:28:34.921
— This year was Kkokkalcorn. — Oh, Kkokkalcorn!
The one I made. Kkokkalcorn. — Kkokkalcorn.

01:28:34.922 --> 01:28:36.322
Kkokkalcorn, Kkokkalcorn.

01:28:36.822 --> 01:28:42.822
— Kkokkalcorn! — Time flies. Before the day—no,
year—ends, ja, let's talk about life's little joys.

01:28:46.842 --> 01:28:48.453
— Joys in life… — ‘Doodles’?!

01:28:48.642 --> 01:28:51.364
— Me! — ‘Fishing’?! — Applied bleach? — ‘Bleach’!

01:28:51.402 --> 01:28:55.569
— Rock? — Go do some laundry with bleach. —
Ah, I'm currently — ‘Fishing’?!

01:28:55.682 --> 01:28:58.942
— It's only been an hour! — Take a picture!

01:28:59.022 --> 01:29:01.542
One hour limit, limit— one hour, one hour

01:29:02.662 --> 01:29:06.061
— You can raise your right hand anytime. —
Okay, right hand!

01:29:06.062 --> 01:29:12.062
Ja, let's talk about life's little joys. Ja,
what are yours these days?

01:29:12.542 --> 01:29:13.942
I'd like to know.

01:29:14.402 --> 01:29:17.421
— I've got it, you know. — What is it? — I'm
really into saunas lately.

01:29:17.422 --> 01:29:19.999
— Saunas are really trendy lately. — You go a lot.

01:29:20.000 --> 01:29:21.461
— I make things trendy! — Why?!

01:29:21.462 --> 01:29:24.301
— They're booming. — Why is everything I do trendy?

01:29:24.302 --> 01:29:25.702
Why?

01:29:26.422 --> 01:29:28.781
You look exhausted, hyung. Ask for help! Okay,

01:29:28.782 --> 01:29:34.262
— There's Namdaemun Market in Seoul… — So, anyway,
whenever I go to the sauna — I'll help you.

01:29:34.442 --> 01:29:38.701
I saw a video recommended on YouTube about
buying sauna supplies there.

01:29:38.702 --> 01:29:40.102
Oh, really?

01:29:40.842 --> 01:29:42.961
— Like exfoliating mitts… — What are you buying?

01:29:42.962 --> 01:29:46.441
— Scrubbing towels? — and exfoliating soap.
Soap that helps remove dead skin.

01:29:46.442 --> 01:29:48.321
— Those mitts… — Gua sha, things like that.

01:29:48.322 --> 01:29:52.933
There are disposable ones with scrub in
them. You put one on, then scrub like this.

01:29:53.862 --> 01:29:55.262
It's disposable.

01:29:56.500 --> 01:29:59.500
Four or five in a pack. One use, then throw it away.

01:29:59.722 --> 01:30:02.161
This scrub smells good and is good for the skin too.

01:30:02.162 --> 01:30:03.562
Do you exfoliate?

01:30:03.822 --> 01:30:05.378
Bamby? Do you do this often?

01:30:05.922 --> 01:30:11.422
Not often. What I like is alternating
between the hot and cold baths.

01:30:11.562 --> 01:30:17.562
I recently learned the Japanese word ‘totonoi.’ It's that
calm, relaxed feeling after going between hot and cold.

01:30:20.802 --> 01:30:24.521
Apparently there's a term for it. I didn't
know the word. I just liked doing it.

01:30:24.522 --> 01:30:26.021
— It calms you? — No, I feel…

01:30:26.022 --> 01:30:32.022
It's more like a runner's high. They call it totonoi. I
loved doing it, and now apparently it's really popular.

01:30:36.682 --> 01:30:39.062
I heard it's good for recovery—your body.

01:30:39.222 --> 01:30:44.666
— For muscle recovery. — I go all in on things. I
liked Pyongyang cold noodles before anyone else!

01:30:44.742 --> 01:30:46.282
Our hyung liked it first.

01:30:46.922 --> 01:30:48.621
— It was famous then! — Already!

01:30:48.622 --> 01:30:51.455
But I liked it even before it became hot like that.

01:30:51.882 --> 01:30:54.461
— Seriously! — Liking things before they're hot.

01:30:54.462 --> 01:30:57.541
— First of all, I really, I really... —
You've got a good eye. A good eye.

01:30:57.542 --> 01:30:58.921
Joys you keep to yourself…

01:30:58.922 --> 01:31:00.901
All my hobbies are trendy! Let's try.

01:31:00.902 --> 01:31:04.081
Then I'd like to get a sense of our Bonggu's
abilities here.

01:31:04.082 --> 01:31:06.481
— Let's try predicting the future once. — Next.

01:31:06.482 --> 01:31:09.302
— Next trend? — Like Dubai chewy cookies.

01:31:09.422 --> 01:31:11.081
— Predict one! — Food? — Anything!

01:31:11.082 --> 01:31:12.881
Anything, anything, it'll be trendy.

01:31:12.882 --> 01:31:15.461
— That's trendy. — Saunas, definitely.

01:31:15.462 --> 01:31:16.501
— Impress me! — Saunas are…

01:31:16.502 --> 01:31:18.261
— Saunas are peaking! — Hey! Hey!

01:31:18.262 --> 01:31:20.041
— Since grade school. — More and more…

01:31:20.042 --> 01:31:25.101
— Get this right and I'll admit it. — Already popular!
Ja, Pyongyang naengmyeon, running… — I liked both!

01:31:25.102 --> 01:31:28.321
— Pyongyang? — Naengmyeon and running. A running boom.

01:31:28.322 --> 01:31:30.741
— Running had a boom. — But running…

01:31:30.742 --> 01:31:32.941
— He started after the boom. — Listen to me!
— Running…

01:31:32.942 --> 01:31:34.561
— You're late. — Hiking's old!

01:31:34.562 --> 01:31:39.081
— Hey, listen up—hiking, hiking, hiking —
You like hiking, too.

01:31:39.082 --> 01:31:40.801
— Already trending. — After the boom! — I…

01:31:40.802 --> 01:31:44.042
But hiking— It'll have another wave. A big one.

01:31:44.462 --> 01:31:49.101
So basically, when a trend comes along, it's
like the equipment comes along with it.

01:31:49.102 --> 01:31:55.102
— With running, the vests and sunglasses
became trendy, too. — Goods, goods

01:31:58.442 --> 01:32:04.201
When running takes off, the gear does, too. People get
into the hobby because collecting all that gear is fun.

01:32:04.202 --> 01:32:06.022
Items... Ah.

01:32:08.442 --> 01:32:11.662
So I predict a hiking-gear boom.

01:32:11.782 --> 01:32:16.241
I'm just letting you know in advance Maybe not
as big as running, but I think it's coming.

01:32:16.242 --> 01:32:18.762
